1
00:04:18,296 --> 00:04:22,028
Far away, on a quiet hillside,
there stood a house.

2
00:04:22,681 --> 00:04:26,579
A tiny house with a tiled roof,
painted bright white.

3
00:04:27,157 --> 00:04:33,493
A father, a mother and their
little boy lived there happily.

4
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,916
The father was a jeep driver.

5
00:04:37,029 --> 00:04:40,244
One day, when the father went
to the plantation to carry a load,

6
00:04:40,477 --> 00:04:42,509
an elephant trampled him to death.

7
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:45,733
And just like that, the mother
and child were left alone.

8
00:04:46,037 --> 00:04:49,684
Neither the villagers nor
their own relatives cared about them.

9
00:04:49,765 --> 00:04:52,837
Blame and poverty were too much to bear...

10
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:55,789
so, they left that house one day...

11
00:04:55,869 --> 00:04:58,941
and got into a lorry bound for the city.

12
00:04:59,021 --> 00:05:00,053
A lorry?

13
00:05:00,261 --> 00:05:02,325
Oh no, not a lorry... a bus.

14
00:05:02,565 --> 00:05:04,005
A blue one.

15
00:05:04,797 --> 00:05:09,052
There were trains and
buildings that touched the sky...

16
00:05:09,133 --> 00:05:13,197
cars and scooters of a kind
we had never seen before.

17
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:15,869
Mom, look! A scooter!

18
00:05:17,884 --> 00:05:18,813
Bath time?

19
00:05:18,893 --> 00:05:19,821
Okay.

20
00:05:51,548 --> 00:05:53,036
[whistles]

21
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:13,308
What the hell!?

22
00:06:13,716 --> 00:06:15,364
Be careful!

23
00:06:19,461 --> 00:06:20,820
How do I look?

24
00:06:22,116 --> 00:06:24,372
So, you're leaving without telling me?

25
00:06:24,453 --> 00:06:25,500
No...

26
00:06:25,581 --> 00:06:27,092
I was coming to see you.

27
00:06:41,756 --> 00:06:43,869
Call me once you're out.

28
00:06:43,949 --> 00:06:46,909
You’ve no idea what I went
through to cut down your sentence.

29
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:50,004
I even had to actually
go around begging people.

30
00:06:50,085 --> 00:06:52,389
Forget the lawyer's fee.

31
00:06:52,469 --> 00:06:54,268
Consider it part of the advance.

32
00:06:54,732 --> 00:06:57,148
We can earn it back once we're out.

33
00:06:59,036 --> 00:07:00,987
It won’t be like jail...

34
00:07:01,068 --> 00:07:03,548
Out there, 'Shamnatha'
won’t be around to save you.

35
00:07:04,083 --> 00:07:05,684
But just relax.

36
00:07:05,764 --> 00:07:08,475
Shamnatha will be out soon enough.

37
00:07:08,698 --> 00:07:10,234
You may leave now.

38
00:07:10,573 --> 00:07:11,229
Hey...

39
00:07:11,468 --> 00:07:13,051
I said you may leave!

40
00:07:17,173 --> 00:07:17,941
Hey!

41
00:07:18,245 --> 00:07:19,589
Make sure you call me.

42
00:07:28,678 --> 00:07:30,478
Put in a pinch more salt.

43
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:35,974
Here are your belongings,

44
00:07:36,054 --> 00:07:37,804
along with the salary
you’ve earned so far.

45
00:07:38,932 --> 00:07:40,885
Take good care of the child, okay?

46
00:07:42,325 --> 00:07:44,357
This is the NGO I mentioned.

47
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,379
If you go there, they'll arrange a job.

48
00:07:47,806 --> 00:07:49,342
I've already spoken to them.

49
00:07:51,829 --> 00:07:53,156
Why don’t you eat
something before you leave?

50
00:07:53,236 --> 00:07:53,828
No...

51
00:07:53,908 --> 00:07:55,892
his uncle will be waiting for us outside.

52
00:07:55,972 --> 00:07:58,044
Which uncle?
Has any of them cared so far?

53
00:07:58,125 --> 00:08:00,268
I shouldn't have to explain this to you.

54
00:08:00,773 --> 00:08:02,245
Start living responsibly.

55
00:08:02,326 --> 00:08:05,669
It’s these innocent kids who
suffer for the wrongs you’ve done.

56
00:08:36,172 --> 00:08:37,357
Puppy!

57
00:08:37,822 --> 00:08:38,765
It's a dog.

58
00:08:39,164 --> 00:08:40,509
Dog!

59
00:08:47,909 --> 00:08:50,101
'SHAMNATHA'

60
00:10:29,127 --> 00:10:30,359
Ticket? Ticket?

61
00:10:31,334 --> 00:10:33,014
What is this, Mom?

62
00:10:34,006 --> 00:10:35,302
I’ll tell you later.

63
00:10:35,382 --> 00:10:36,997
Where to, huh?

64
00:10:38,247 --> 00:10:38,919
Hmm?

65
00:10:39,495 --> 00:10:40,455
Where to?

66
00:10:42,423 --> 00:10:44,375
You don't even know where to go?

67
00:10:47,003 --> 00:10:50,077
'BALAN-THE BOY'

68
00:11:12,815 --> 00:11:15,887
-Sudheer... one tea, please.
-Oh, tea?

69
00:11:22,318 --> 00:11:23,509
You want tea?

70
00:11:25,151 --> 00:11:28,062
Sudheer, how long does it
take to get some chutney?

71
00:11:29,334 --> 00:11:30,662
Oh, chutney.

72
00:11:51,517 --> 00:11:52,702
170 rupees.

73
00:11:52,782 --> 00:11:54,062
Brother...

74
00:11:54,143 --> 00:11:56,327
we don’t have any money.

75
00:11:56,407 --> 00:11:57,454
No money?

76
00:11:58,109 --> 00:12:00,221
And yet you gobbled
up everything in sight?

77
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,886
We were hungry.

78
00:12:08,366 --> 00:12:09,566
You can go.

79
00:12:12,221 --> 00:12:14,269
Brother, can I get some work here?

80
00:12:14,350 --> 00:12:15,166
Work?

81
00:12:15,246 --> 00:12:17,333
Yeah... I’ll do anything.

82
00:12:17,511 --> 00:12:19,831
Well, I barely earn enough...

83
00:12:19,912 --> 00:12:21,582
to get by.

84
00:12:21,663 --> 00:12:23,519
I don’t need wages, brother...

85
00:12:23,599 --> 00:12:25,071
just something to eat.

86
00:12:25,470 --> 00:12:27,878
I’ll sleep anywhere...
on a bench or something.

87
00:12:27,959 --> 00:12:29,846
We’re from Idukki.

88
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:31,751
When his father...

89
00:12:31,831 --> 00:12:34,200
went to the plantation to carry loads...

90
00:12:34,487 --> 00:12:36,455
an elephant trampled him to death.

91
00:12:38,004 --> 00:12:39,407
Left with no one,

92
00:12:39,487 --> 00:12:41,220
we had no choice but to leave home.

93
00:12:41,454 --> 00:12:43,198
We wandered from place to place.

94
00:12:43,487 --> 00:12:45,470
I don’t even know where to go now.

95
00:12:46,406 --> 00:12:47,687
What’s your name?

96
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:48,294
Indhu.

97
00:12:48,375 --> 00:12:48,950
And his?

98
00:12:49,031 --> 00:12:50,294
Abh-- Abhijith Kumar.

99
00:12:52,247 --> 00:12:54,006
Abhijith Kumar...

100
00:12:54,343 --> 00:12:56,535
I’ve already explained my situation.

101
00:12:56,616 --> 00:12:58,999
I can’t help you here. Better you go.

102
00:12:59,597 --> 00:13:01,373
I’ll do any work...

103
00:13:01,710 --> 00:13:03,886
I can wash plates or sweep...

104
00:13:03,966 --> 00:13:05,398
Please leave for God's sake, dear.

105
00:13:05,478 --> 00:13:07,414
I'm already pretty tied up.

106
00:14:25,134 --> 00:14:27,182
-Why are you late?
-I overslept.

107
00:14:27,263 --> 00:14:28,038
Oh, is it?

108
00:15:11,022 --> 00:15:12,606
Who’s this lady, Brother Sudheer?

109
00:15:12,687 --> 00:15:15,110
Whoever she is,
she’s someone dear to me, Sunny.

110
00:15:17,638 --> 00:15:19,558
And what’s the name of this “dear” person?

111
00:15:19,638 --> 00:15:20,303
Indhu.

112
00:15:20,622 --> 00:15:21,398
What now?

113
00:15:21,479 --> 00:15:22,590
Nothing.

114
00:15:23,022 --> 00:15:25,262
By “dear,” do you mean you married her?

115
00:15:25,502 --> 00:15:26,590
No...

116
00:15:26,894 --> 00:15:28,942
If that happens, you’ll get an invitation!

117
00:15:29,198 --> 00:15:30,510
Didn’t you get what you asked for?

118
00:15:30,591 --> 00:15:31,486
Go on, go!

119
00:15:33,279 --> 00:15:34,214
Lucky old man!

120
00:15:38,845 --> 00:15:39,933
Indhu...

121
00:15:43,382 --> 00:15:45,270
You don’t have to sleep here anymore.

122
00:15:45,386 --> 00:15:46,758
Come home...

123
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:49,238
Be my daughter and grandson.

124
00:15:50,022 --> 00:15:50,966
Here you go.

125
00:16:22,253 --> 00:16:23,518
Indhu?

126
00:16:23,598 --> 00:16:24,846
Indhu?!

127
00:16:27,422 --> 00:16:28,781
Abhijith, dear?

128
00:16:41,271 --> 00:16:44,775
Mom, why did we leave
that grandpa’s tea shop?

129
00:16:46,151 --> 00:16:48,071
All we need is each other.

130
00:16:48,582 --> 00:16:50,439
No one else in between.

131
00:16:51,375 --> 00:16:52,110
Hmm?

132
00:16:52,446 --> 00:16:53,055
Hmm.

133
00:17:03,807 --> 00:17:06,942
Seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven, twelve...

134
00:17:07,134 --> 00:17:09,983
Twenty-two, twenty-three,
twenty-four, twenty-five...

135
00:17:10,333 --> 00:17:11,471
How many boats did you see?

136
00:17:13,182 --> 00:17:14,574
Twenty-five.

137
00:17:16,895 --> 00:17:17,903
Mom...

138
00:17:18,654 --> 00:17:20,590
what’s our new story?

139
00:17:21,198 --> 00:17:21,935
I’ll tell you.

140
00:17:22,015 --> 00:17:23,790
And what’s my new name?

141
00:17:25,935 --> 00:17:27,711
Adhiseshan.

142
00:17:28,791 --> 00:17:29,910
Did you like it?

143
00:17:29,991 --> 00:17:31,383
Yes, super!

144
00:17:31,464 --> 00:17:37,909
♪ Like leaves floating along ♪

145
00:17:38,971 --> 00:17:41,362
♪ Two wandering souls ♪

146
00:17:41,446 --> 00:17:46,539
♪ Lonely shadows ♪

147
00:17:49,284 --> 00:17:55,795
♪ Across the trails where
shadows stretch, daylight faded ♪

148
00:17:59,014 --> 00:18:05,270
♪ And they turn into nightly tales
by wayside inns ♪

149
00:18:19,806 --> 00:18:22,319
Your ID card still hasn’t come from home?

150
00:18:22,743 --> 00:18:24,294
Don’t you dare show up without it!

151
00:18:24,455 --> 00:18:25,382
Understood!?

152
00:18:26,332 --> 00:18:27,303
Get it done fast.

153
00:18:27,909 --> 00:18:32,860
♪ In a nameless tent burning in silence ♪

154
00:18:37,789 --> 00:18:42,845
♪ And in this endless revelry,
do these disguises still dance on? ♪

155
00:18:43,381 --> 00:18:44,670
Too hot, isn’t it?

156
00:18:47,476 --> 00:18:49,151
How about a beer?

157
00:18:53,421 --> 00:18:54,191
Blood!

158
00:18:54,707 --> 00:18:55,318
Hey!

159
00:18:55,399 --> 00:18:57,030
Your mom's crazy!

160
00:18:57,111 --> 00:19:02,333
♪ Barren trees swaying
only for one another ♪

161
00:19:05,197 --> 00:19:07,214
♪ The clamor... ♪

162
00:19:07,533 --> 00:19:08,607
Once again.

163
00:19:15,661 --> 00:19:16,623
Mom...

164
00:19:17,373 --> 00:19:19,230
how many more stories do I have to learn?

165
00:19:19,636 --> 00:19:20,351
Plenty...

166
00:19:20,431 --> 00:19:21,438
you still have many to learn.

167
00:19:21,519 --> 00:19:23,943
Hmm... do I have to
remember all the stories I learn?

168
00:19:24,024 --> 00:19:26,070
All those stories...

169
00:19:29,605 --> 00:19:31,797
♪ Where are you off to,
like the wind? ♪

170
00:19:31,877 --> 00:19:34,373
♪ Where are you off to,
like the cloud? ♪

171
00:19:34,453 --> 00:19:39,268
♪ Is it to reap the great
rain in the fields of the sky? ♪

172
00:19:39,349 --> 00:19:42,093
♪ O hands, legs and eyes ♪

173
00:19:42,173 --> 00:19:44,069
♪ Where are you all off to? ♪

174
00:19:44,150 --> 00:19:48,085
♪ Chasing the fleeting deer, a mirage ♪

175
00:19:48,263 --> 00:19:49,911
Didn’t I warn you already?

176
00:19:49,992 --> 00:19:52,439
Don’t talk about us to anyone.

177
00:19:53,085 --> 00:19:54,567
And certainly not the police.

178
00:19:54,648 --> 00:19:55,494
Got me?

179
00:20:00,551 --> 00:20:02,118
There’s my aunt’s son.

180
00:20:02,199 --> 00:20:03,711
He's a divorcee.

181
00:20:03,792 --> 00:20:05,814
Shall I see about an alliance for you?

182
00:20:06,911 --> 00:20:08,767
Think it through and let me know.

183
00:20:11,327 --> 00:20:12,911
If you’re willing...

184
00:20:13,966 --> 00:20:15,581
I’ll take care of you.

185
00:20:16,830 --> 00:20:17,774
And him too.

186
00:20:19,047 --> 00:20:21,174
Like my... own son.

187
00:20:30,898 --> 00:20:32,545
Not done yet?

188
00:20:34,306 --> 00:20:35,650
Move that a bit.

189
00:21:05,716 --> 00:21:06,772
Hello?

190
00:21:07,852 --> 00:21:08,748
Hello!

191
00:21:08,829 --> 00:21:10,004
Are you working here now?

192
00:21:10,283 --> 00:21:13,034
Don’t you recognise me?
We’ve met at Sudheer bro’s tea shop.

193
00:21:13,883 --> 00:21:15,619
Super! That didn’t work, Sunny!

194
00:21:15,699 --> 00:21:17,426
Wait, wait! I know her.

195
00:21:17,507 --> 00:21:18,307
Is it true, Mary?

196
00:21:18,387 --> 00:21:19,163
Mary?

197
00:21:19,324 --> 00:21:21,116
Oh really? You said you know her?

198
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:24,229
Yeah… it wasn’t Mary.
It was some Hindu name.

199
00:21:24,310 --> 00:21:25,285
Then you’ve got the wrong person.

200
00:21:25,366 --> 00:21:27,341
No way, brother.
That boy was with her too.

201
00:21:27,422 --> 00:21:29,037
Where were you working before this?

202
00:21:29,117 --> 00:21:30,517
Nowhere.

203
00:21:30,598 --> 00:21:31,373
Why not?

204
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:34,028
It's only now that
I've had to start working.

205
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:35,820
Brother...

206
00:21:35,901 --> 00:21:37,532
Something feels off about this.

207
00:21:37,612 --> 00:21:39,436
Stop overthinking.
Unload the goods and leave.

208
00:21:39,517 --> 00:21:42,116
Wait, wait. This feels fishy.
Repeat your name.

209
00:21:42,284 --> 00:21:43,308
Mary...

210
00:21:43,389 --> 00:21:44,364
Mary Luca.

211
00:21:45,260 --> 00:21:46,412
And the boy’s name?

212
00:21:46,492 --> 00:21:47,211
Benny.

213
00:21:48,284 --> 00:21:49,677
Show me your voter ID. Come on!

214
00:21:49,757 --> 00:21:51,717
Damn… that’s what
she lost in the landslide.

215
00:21:52,443 --> 00:21:53,858
Landslide?

216
00:21:56,036 --> 00:21:58,693
Forget that. Your husband’s name?
What did he do?

217
00:21:58,774 --> 00:22:00,781
Luca. He was a mechanic.

218
00:22:03,291 --> 00:22:05,373
Your house… the one that got buried...

219
00:22:05,453 --> 00:22:06,701
what colour was it?

220
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:08,211
White.

221
00:22:08,572 --> 00:22:09,549
White?

222
00:22:09,741 --> 00:22:11,853
Err... Tiled roof? Or was it a terrace?

223
00:22:12,908 --> 00:22:14,204
Tiled roof.

224
00:22:14,284 --> 00:22:15,612
You heard that.

225
00:22:15,693 --> 00:22:17,085
Did your husband own a vehicle?

226
00:22:17,165 --> 00:22:17,757
Yeah...

227
00:22:18,004 --> 00:22:19,237
A scooter.

228
00:22:19,404 --> 00:22:20,859
A scooter, right?

229
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:21,867
Stay right here.

230
00:22:21,948 --> 00:22:23,604
-Brother, come with me.
-What is it?

231
00:22:23,859 --> 00:22:26,324
Well, she seems like a pro at lying.

232
00:22:27,075 --> 00:22:27,924
Hey, kid!

233
00:22:29,588 --> 00:22:31,395
Turn this way.

234
00:22:32,644 --> 00:22:34,212
What’s your name, dear?

235
00:22:35,013 --> 00:22:35,988
Benny.

236
00:22:36,236 --> 00:22:37,547
And your mom’s name?

237
00:22:38,124 --> 00:22:39,099
Mary.

238
00:22:40,188 --> 00:22:40,763
So...

239
00:22:40,844 --> 00:22:41,884
Where is your father?

240
00:22:42,236 --> 00:22:43,355
He's dead.

241
00:22:45,364 --> 00:22:46,676
What was your dad’s name?

242
00:22:47,124 --> 00:22:48,452
Hmm... Luca.

243
00:22:49,731 --> 00:22:51,491
Haven’t you seen me before, boy?

244
00:22:51,684 --> 00:22:53,115
At a tea shop?

245
00:22:55,827 --> 00:22:56,451
No!

246
00:23:00,651 --> 00:23:02,795
What was your mother's job earlier?

247
00:23:03,020 --> 00:23:04,308
She wasn't working.

248
00:23:06,315 --> 00:23:07,964
You clever little boy!

249
00:23:09,556 --> 00:23:11,972
Do you remember your house’s colour?

250
00:23:12,371 --> 00:23:13,779
-Yes.
-What was it?

251
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:14,459
White.

252
00:23:16,164 --> 00:23:17,715
Tiled roof or terrace?

253
00:23:18,596 --> 00:23:19,572
Tiled roof.

254
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:24,436
Your dad had a vehicle?

255
00:23:25,116 --> 00:23:25,788
Yes.

256
00:23:27,148 --> 00:23:28,444
A...

257
00:23:28,979 --> 00:23:30,260
A yellow scooter.

258
00:23:30,452 --> 00:23:32,051
Super! Come here, you!

259
00:23:32,132 --> 00:23:33,707
Just troubling people for no reason!

260
00:23:33,788 --> 00:23:35,579
-Unload the stuff and get lost, Sunny!
-Wait a sec.

261
00:23:35,724 --> 00:23:37,755
You’re Christian, right?
Say a couple of Bible verses.

262
00:23:37,836 --> 00:23:38,780
Just come!

263
00:23:38,860 --> 00:23:41,092
Enough with your nonsense questions!

264
00:23:41,285 --> 00:23:42,637
She’s a fraud! You’ll regret this!

265
00:23:42,718 --> 00:23:44,267
Dear, she’s not right in the head.

266
00:23:44,348 --> 00:23:46,621
Don’t let this stop you
from coming to work.

267
00:24:08,028 --> 00:24:10,540
Bye, bye!

268
00:24:10,621 --> 00:24:11,740
Bye!

269
00:24:16,156 --> 00:24:18,028
Go change your clothes.

270
00:24:19,293 --> 00:24:21,388
Vandana, give Vasudev some milk.

271
00:24:21,469 --> 00:24:22,725
Yes, right away, sister.

272
00:24:24,357 --> 00:24:25,941
Give some to Manu as well.

273
00:24:26,229 --> 00:24:28,533
That's fine, sister. I’ll give him later.

274
00:24:28,613 --> 00:24:29,957
No, do it now.

275
00:24:41,493 --> 00:24:44,325
He’s so excited about coming there.

276
00:24:44,932 --> 00:24:46,836
No, he just got back from school.

277
00:24:47,124 --> 00:24:49,892
I’ll hand over the documents to Ajayan.

278
00:24:50,508 --> 00:24:51,948
No, no.

279
00:24:52,821 --> 00:24:54,309
I won’t forget.

280
00:24:54,389 --> 00:24:55,765
Vandana...

281
00:24:56,285 --> 00:24:58,109
These are Vasu’s documents.

282
00:24:58,190 --> 00:25:00,509
Get two copies made to send to the Gulf.

283
00:25:01,427 --> 00:25:03,107
I’ve already put in a
word for your husband.

284
00:25:03,188 --> 00:25:05,044
Why keep struggling in Delhi?

285
00:25:34,684 --> 00:25:35,836
What happened?

286
00:25:35,917 --> 00:25:39,052
The school rickshaw Vasudev was in…
it met with an accident…

287
00:26:01,341 --> 00:26:03,853
[school rickshaw accident news]

288
00:26:38,741 --> 00:26:39,909
Did I lose it?

289
00:26:40,012 --> 00:26:41,325
Where is it?

290
00:26:41,629 --> 00:26:43,229
I kept it right here.

291
00:26:43,469 --> 00:26:44,380
Is it gone?

292
00:27:47,273 --> 00:27:49,545
-Your name is Sherly, right?
-Yes.

293
00:27:49,825 --> 00:27:51,272
Even though your agency's shut,

294
00:27:51,356 --> 00:27:54,033
I'm sending you there as I've
been told you're experienced.

295
00:27:54,822 --> 00:27:56,646
I slipped off my scooter,

296
00:27:56,730 --> 00:27:58,329
so walking’s a bit
difficult at the moment.

297
00:27:58,500 --> 00:28:00,529
Once I recover, I’ll come there.

298
00:28:00,879 --> 00:28:02,903
I've been put in charge
of everything out there.

299
00:28:03,117 --> 00:28:04,413
So make sure everything’s
handled properly.

300
00:28:04,493 --> 00:28:05,092
Alright.

301
00:28:13,193 --> 00:28:14,818
Only an old woman lives there.

302
00:28:14,902 --> 00:28:16,629
All of her children are settled abroad.

303
00:28:37,507 --> 00:28:38,938
The house won’t be locked.

304
00:28:39,019 --> 00:28:42,778
Go in and tell her Iype
sent you to look after her.

305
00:28:45,229 --> 00:28:48,013
Also, at 1 p.m., her son
will call from England.

306
00:28:48,276 --> 00:28:50,459
He’ll guide you further.

307
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:55,997
Listen, that old lady doesn’t really talk.

308
00:28:56,081 --> 00:28:57,697
She’s a little hard to put up with…

309
00:28:57,781 --> 00:28:59,428
you’ll have to manage.

310
00:29:23,829 --> 00:29:24,821
Take off your slippers.

311
00:30:08,061 --> 00:30:09,574
[phone ringing]

312
00:30:14,637 --> 00:30:15,580
-Hello?
-Hello...

313
00:30:15,661 --> 00:30:17,038
This is Joseph speaking.

314
00:30:17,357 --> 00:30:19,438
Iype told me about you.

315
00:30:19,518 --> 00:30:21,070
You know, mom is an odd character.

316
00:30:21,301 --> 00:30:22,821
She's a bit tough to handle.

317
00:30:23,038 --> 00:30:24,549
Hope you guys figure it out.

318
00:30:24,923 --> 00:30:26,955
So, you can choose any room you like...

319
00:30:27,036 --> 00:30:28,036
and you can live there.

320
00:30:28,117 --> 00:30:30,349
I suppose Iype’s already
told you about the salary.

321
00:30:30,468 --> 00:30:32,828
And I’ll call you on the
first of every month at 1 pm.

322
00:30:32,908 --> 00:30:34,396
Be attentive to everything out there.

323
00:30:34,477 --> 00:30:36,445
Where were you working before this?

324
00:30:36,526 --> 00:30:37,821
At an old-age home--

325
00:30:37,901 --> 00:30:38,781
Yeah, yeah, whatever!

326
00:30:38,989 --> 00:30:40,269
Sherly, right?

327
00:30:40,541 --> 00:30:41,470
Yes.

328
00:30:53,509 --> 00:30:55,477
Who the hell are you, wretch?

329
00:30:55,750 --> 00:30:57,061
Sh--Sherly.

330
00:30:57,142 --> 00:30:58,366
I’m here to look after you.

331
00:30:58,446 --> 00:31:00,382
Did that prick Iype send you?

332
00:31:00,820 --> 00:31:01,765
Yes.

333
00:31:02,206 --> 00:31:05,854
I’m waiting to put that
scoundrel at my gunpoint!

334
00:31:06,628 --> 00:31:08,293
Please don’t... hurt us.

335
00:31:13,309 --> 00:31:15,101
Is this your son or what!?

336
00:31:16,245 --> 00:31:17,109
Yes.

337
00:31:18,124 --> 00:31:19,765
Where’s his father?

338
00:31:21,196 --> 00:31:22,381
He’s dead.

339
00:31:23,257 --> 00:31:24,313
Good for you!

340
00:31:28,429 --> 00:31:30,477
You’d better behave yourself.

341
00:31:32,893 --> 00:31:35,053
Did you bring me anything to eat?

342
00:31:35,198 --> 00:31:37,741
No… shall I make something for you?

343
00:31:37,989 --> 00:31:38,981
Be quick.

344
00:31:39,062 --> 00:31:40,797
The hungrier I get…

345
00:31:40,973 --> 00:31:42,237
the madder I become!

346
00:31:43,925 --> 00:31:44,998
Go on!

347
00:32:17,915 --> 00:32:19,179
Mom…

348
00:32:19,740 --> 00:32:22,348
Is that grandma going to hurt us?

349
00:32:25,284 --> 00:32:26,565
You never know.

350
00:32:28,069 --> 00:32:29,413
Scared?

351
00:32:30,940 --> 00:32:32,253
A little.

352
00:32:34,821 --> 00:32:36,292
Don’t worry.

353
00:32:40,348 --> 00:32:42,813
Are you gonna hurt her, mom?

354
00:32:45,108 --> 00:32:46,341
Let me see.

355
00:32:48,828 --> 00:32:50,379
If it comes to that...

356
00:33:00,628 --> 00:33:01,477
Grandma…

357
00:33:01,558 --> 00:33:03,820
Grandma, what happened? What do you want?

358
00:33:03,901 --> 00:33:05,149
Where’s your medicine?

359
00:33:09,013 --> 00:33:10,036
-This one?
-No...

360
00:33:16,133 --> 00:33:17,285
This?

361
00:33:21,212 --> 00:33:22,316
Or this one?

362
00:33:22,396 --> 00:33:23,196
Yes...

363
00:33:58,714 --> 00:34:01,658
I was told that Grandma
doesn’t talk to anyone.

364
00:34:02,746 --> 00:34:04,977
That’s only for that
blockhead son of mine.

365
00:34:05,811 --> 00:34:07,827
Why won’t you speak to anyone?

366
00:34:07,907 --> 00:34:09,706
Do you need every damn detail?

367
00:34:10,491 --> 00:34:11,322
No.

368
00:34:13,219 --> 00:34:16,418
My husband was a freedom fighter.

369
00:34:16,755 --> 00:34:19,714
Not some coward who
stayed silent, mind you.

370
00:34:19,795 --> 00:34:22,050
He hunted down the British!

371
00:34:22,130 --> 00:34:25,714
After driving them out
and winning our freedom...

372
00:34:25,795 --> 00:34:28,579
his own son went back
there to work like a slave.

373
00:34:28,659 --> 00:34:31,395
And you expect me to
cuddle a fellow like that!?

374
00:34:31,475 --> 00:34:34,340
I don’t want that
useless guy in my sight!

375
00:34:34,779 --> 00:34:37,803
Still, how can you not speak
to him for 15 long years?

376
00:34:39,386 --> 00:34:40,618
Back then…

377
00:34:40,731 --> 00:34:42,482
as they couldn’t capture my husband…

378
00:34:42,562 --> 00:34:45,393
the British police arrested me instead.

379
00:34:45,474 --> 00:34:47,289
I was locked up for six months.

380
00:34:47,385 --> 00:34:48,762
Tied up and beaten.

381
00:34:48,842 --> 00:34:50,378
Tortured in every possible way.

382
00:34:50,458 --> 00:34:51,770
Forced to drink urine.

383
00:34:51,850 --> 00:34:53,737
My body left covered in wounds.

384
00:34:53,818 --> 00:34:55,034
Chilli powder rubbed into them.

385
00:34:55,114 --> 00:34:56,601
Even my nails were torn out.

386
00:34:56,683 --> 00:34:58,689
Still, I did not utter a single word.

387
00:34:58,827 --> 00:35:01,050
And you think I’ll crack for my son!?

388
00:35:06,242 --> 00:35:08,306
What did you say your name was?

389
00:35:09,693 --> 00:35:10,265
Sherly.

390
00:35:15,066 --> 00:35:16,675
Ranjini… your husband?

391
00:35:16,756 --> 00:35:18,427
He’s in the Gulf.

392
00:35:25,282 --> 00:35:26,739
This address…

393
00:35:26,819 --> 00:35:28,275
it’s quite far from here.

394
00:35:28,578 --> 00:35:29,874
It’s my mom’s house.

395
00:35:29,955 --> 00:35:31,554
She lives there alone.

396
00:35:31,635 --> 00:35:34,026
And there aren’t any
good schools nearby either…

397
00:35:34,107 --> 00:35:35,034
Fine, fine.

398
00:35:56,260 --> 00:35:58,708
Grandma, are you going to shoot us?

399
00:35:59,923 --> 00:36:01,875
That hasn’t crossed my mind yet.

400
00:36:01,955 --> 00:36:03,691
But if I must, I will!

401
00:36:03,772 --> 00:36:05,923
Then we’ll mix poison for you!

402
00:36:06,188 --> 00:36:07,171
Oh, please!

403
00:36:07,252 --> 00:36:09,532
Do you think I’d blindly swallow
whatever your mother gives me?

404
00:36:09,612 --> 00:36:11,036
But you wouldn’t even know.

405
00:36:11,117 --> 00:36:13,379
What if we mix it in your coffee?

406
00:36:13,460 --> 00:36:14,252
Huh?

407
00:36:22,234 --> 00:36:23,770
I don’t want it.

408
00:36:23,851 --> 00:36:24,748
There’s no poison.

409
00:36:24,828 --> 00:36:26,756
I only said that to give him some peace.

410
00:36:26,837 --> 00:36:28,300
And there goes my peace!

411
00:36:28,380 --> 00:36:29,892
Shall I take a sip first?

412
00:36:30,235 --> 00:36:31,796
No! Give it to me.

413
00:36:31,877 --> 00:36:33,388
If I die, so be it!

414
00:37:01,084 --> 00:37:03,755
Listen to your teacher
and study well, okay?

415
00:37:05,084 --> 00:37:07,115
-Don’t forget what I told you.
-Yes.

416
00:37:07,196 --> 00:37:09,100
Only we need to know who we are.

417
00:37:09,180 --> 00:37:10,364
No one else does.

418
00:37:12,658 --> 00:37:14,098
Vasudev, right?

419
00:37:15,620 --> 00:37:16,628
Come.

420
00:37:35,284 --> 00:37:37,859
Vasudev, wait here.
I’ll be back in a minute.

421
00:37:43,698 --> 00:37:45,178
[school bell rings]

422
00:37:50,611 --> 00:37:53,683
Students, we have a new
admission today - Vasudev.

423
00:37:53,764 --> 00:37:54,787
Vasudev...

424
00:37:54,868 --> 00:37:56,355
introduce yourself.

425
00:38:11,146 --> 00:38:11,946
Silence!

426
00:38:12,548 --> 00:38:13,732
Tell them your name.

427
00:38:13,812 --> 00:38:16,195
Also, where you’re from
and your parents’ names.

428
00:38:16,276 --> 00:38:18,020
Can you tell us where your house is?

429
00:38:21,235 --> 00:38:23,218
What’s your father’s name?

430
00:38:25,387 --> 00:38:26,955
Your mother’s name?

431
00:38:28,004 --> 00:38:28,593
Kavitha!

432
00:38:28,674 --> 00:38:29,236
Indhu!

433
00:38:29,316 --> 00:38:29,827
Vandana!

434
00:38:30,468 --> 00:38:31,036
Farzana!

435
00:38:31,692 --> 00:38:32,300
My dear!

436
00:38:39,898 --> 00:38:40,747
Okay.

437
00:38:41,020 --> 00:38:42,172
Go sit over there.

438
00:38:44,755 --> 00:38:46,051
Students...

439
00:38:46,132 --> 00:38:48,723
we’re going to learn a poem, okay?

440
00:38:49,162 --> 00:38:51,754
Green trees, green trees...

441
00:38:51,835 --> 00:38:54,018
Green trees, green trees...

442
00:38:54,196 --> 00:38:56,491
Blue birds, blue birds...

443
00:38:56,572 --> 00:38:59,419
Blue birds, blue birds...

444
00:39:10,419 --> 00:39:11,314
Wait, wait!

445
00:39:11,395 --> 00:39:13,299
Let me check if that old lady is around!

446
00:39:14,716 --> 00:39:15,868
Come, come.

447
00:39:22,804 --> 00:39:24,259
Hurry up, hurry up!

448
00:39:24,707 --> 00:39:26,915
Otherwise it’ll turn into a big scene!

449
00:39:28,300 --> 00:39:29,859
Quick!

450
00:39:29,939 --> 00:39:32,003
We have to get out before she comes!

451
00:39:43,012 --> 00:39:46,276
-Who’s there, you little brats!?
-The mad woman’s here! Run, run!

452
00:39:57,963 --> 00:39:59,515
Are you crazy, you wicked woman?

453
00:39:59,596 --> 00:40:00,955
What if something had
happened to those children?

454
00:40:01,036 --> 00:40:02,116
Wicked woman, huh!?

455
00:40:05,505 --> 00:40:06,986
Mom, poison her!

456
00:40:07,066 --> 00:40:09,218
As if your mom would be alive to do that.

457
00:40:09,298 --> 00:40:11,323
This bullet will go straight through her!

458
00:40:16,563 --> 00:40:17,506
Mom!

459
00:40:21,643 --> 00:40:24,747
It only makes a sound, you dumbass!

460
00:40:24,827 --> 00:40:26,530
It’s just a blank.

461
00:40:26,611 --> 00:40:29,356
Just to scare fools like you.

462
00:40:29,436 --> 00:40:31,355
After all, I'm living here alone.

463
00:40:31,739 --> 00:40:33,675
There’s a rumour that the old lady here

464
00:40:33,755 --> 00:40:35,691
shoots anyone who steps into her yard.

465
00:40:35,932 --> 00:40:37,963
So, not a single thief dares to come near.

466
00:40:38,044 --> 00:40:40,186
Got the trick?

467
00:40:41,524 --> 00:40:43,283
Go get me some tea.

468
00:41:04,284 --> 00:41:05,292
Mom…

469
00:41:06,028 --> 00:41:07,835
I learnt a new song today.

470
00:41:08,924 --> 00:41:09,770
Go ahead, sing it.

471
00:41:09,850 --> 00:41:12,186
♪ Have you seen the key? ♪

472
00:41:12,267 --> 00:41:15,081
♪ The tiny froggy’s key ♪

473
00:41:15,162 --> 00:41:19,849
♪ The key that slipped
while wandering here and there ♪

474
00:41:19,929 --> 00:41:22,793
♪ The key that slipped away ♪

475
00:41:25,403 --> 00:41:28,001
♪ O crab-bro, digging the sand, ♪

476
00:41:28,082 --> 00:41:30,338
♪ Have you seen the key? ♪

477
00:41:30,633 --> 00:41:32,945
♪ Have you seen the key? ♪

478
00:41:33,026 --> 00:41:35,769
♪ While I dig the muddy earth ♪

479
00:41:35,850 --> 00:41:38,682
♪ How could I see your key? ♪

480
00:41:40,852 --> 00:41:43,874
♪ Hey tusker, wearing a golden caparison ♪

481
00:41:43,954 --> 00:41:45,938
♪ Have you seen my key? ♪

482
00:41:46,116 --> 00:41:48,804
♪ Have you seen it at all? ♪

483
00:41:48,885 --> 00:41:51,428
♪ It’s not in the beating drum, ♪

484
00:41:51,509 --> 00:41:53,892
♪ Nor in the bursting crackers ♪

485
00:41:56,378 --> 00:41:59,434
♪ O my egret, have you seen the key, ♪

486
00:41:59,515 --> 00:42:01,498
♪ while hanging on the cattle's tail? ♪

487
00:42:01,579 --> 00:42:06,618
♪ Only the fish popping up
have I seen with my eyes ♪

488
00:42:10,762 --> 00:42:13,419
Where were you working before this?

489
00:42:14,202 --> 00:42:15,322
In Kannur…

490
00:42:15,403 --> 00:42:16,810
at an old-age home.

491
00:42:18,091 --> 00:42:21,723
Why do you take the boy
by the back route to school?

492
00:42:24,217 --> 00:42:27,080
You can have the
school bus stop at the gate.

493
00:42:29,554 --> 00:42:31,154
I understand…

494
00:42:31,234 --> 00:42:32,978
you’re not here to steal.

495
00:42:33,058 --> 00:42:36,777
If you were, you wouldn't
have enrolled him in school.

496
00:42:38,057 --> 00:42:41,417
Anyway, no one will
come looking for you here.

497
00:42:42,602 --> 00:42:43,866
Lay me down.

498
00:42:50,698 --> 00:42:52,186
How’s this?

499
00:42:54,106 --> 00:42:55,914
That’s you, you fool!

500
00:42:56,714 --> 00:42:58,250
This is you, Grandma!

501
00:43:03,001 --> 00:43:04,633
Not that one, the green one.

502
00:43:04,713 --> 00:43:06,921
This one is just to scare people…

503
00:43:07,002 --> 00:43:08,921
and that's to kill them!

504
00:43:15,330 --> 00:43:16,050
[gunfire]

505
00:43:16,731 --> 00:43:17,898
[phone rings]

506
00:43:17,979 --> 00:43:19,594
Hello?
-Hey, Sherly?

507
00:43:19,675 --> 00:43:20,938
Is mom doing well?

508
00:43:21,291 --> 00:43:21,931
Yes.

509
00:43:22,012 --> 00:43:23,787
Does she say anything about us?

510
00:43:24,153 --> 00:43:25,825
She doesn't talk to
anyone at all, though.

511
00:43:25,905 --> 00:43:27,186
Yeah, that's right.

512
00:43:27,267 --> 00:43:28,947
Call Iype if you need any help.

513
00:43:29,027 --> 00:43:29,908
Okay.

514
00:43:31,875 --> 00:43:32,962
Good job.

515
00:43:33,867 --> 00:43:34,810
What?

516
00:43:34,891 --> 00:43:37,051
Good thing you didn’t tell him
I talk to you.

517
00:43:37,300 --> 00:43:38,227
Why?

518
00:43:38,426 --> 00:43:40,602
One less bullet wasted.

519
00:43:40,938 --> 00:43:43,209
♪ O bat hanging from a tree trunk ♪

520
00:43:43,290 --> 00:43:45,666
♪ Did you see my silver key? ♪

521
00:43:45,987 --> 00:43:48,104
♪ It's not in the pitch-dark night ♪

522
00:43:48,722 --> 00:43:51,154
♪ Nor on the roof beam ♪

523
00:43:51,235 --> 00:43:53,969
♪ As the frog went around asking ♪

524
00:43:54,050 --> 00:43:56,298
♪ Stretched out long and flat was ♪

525
00:43:56,379 --> 00:43:58,794
♪ A key like a wriggly water-eel ♪

526
00:43:58,875 --> 00:44:00,970
♪ A key like a wriggly water-eel ♪

527
00:44:01,051 --> 00:44:06,242
♪ Even today,
the tiny frog asks everyone ♪

528
00:44:06,322 --> 00:44:09,128
♪ Croak, croak, did you see the key? ♪

529
00:44:09,210 --> 00:44:11,626
♪ The silver key to my home ♪

530
00:44:11,707 --> 00:44:14,538
♪ Croak, croak, did you see the key? ♪

531
00:44:14,625 --> 00:44:16,952
♪ The glowing firefly key ♪

532
00:44:17,025 --> 00:44:19,842
♪ The glowing firefly key ♪

533
00:44:59,803 --> 00:45:01,522
I was only a little late, huh!?

534
00:45:01,603 --> 00:45:03,907
Why did you wander off
instead of waiting here?

535
00:45:04,204 --> 00:45:04,988
Huh?

536
00:45:14,050 --> 00:45:16,002
From now on, however late I may be...

537
00:45:16,227 --> 00:45:18,147
leave not this place.

538
00:45:18,738 --> 00:45:20,194
Remain here.

539
00:45:22,027 --> 00:45:23,323
Mother will come.

540
00:45:24,753 --> 00:45:25,883
Do you hear me?

541
00:45:30,787 --> 00:45:32,020
And so…

542
00:45:32,100 --> 00:45:35,843
My husband and I hid in a
dark room for seven days…

543
00:45:35,924 --> 00:45:38,435
without food and not even water.

544
00:45:38,762 --> 00:45:40,746
You suffered a lot, didn’t you?

545
00:45:40,827 --> 00:45:43,154
That was absolutely nothing.

546
00:45:45,451 --> 00:45:49,003
Instead of me going on and on,
don’t you have anything to say?

547
00:45:49,084 --> 00:45:51,515
There’s nothing much to say about me.

548
00:45:51,596 --> 00:45:55,292
Then make something up,
just so I can enjoy hearing it.

549
00:45:56,682 --> 00:45:58,491
What about a story?

550
00:45:59,074 --> 00:46:00,483
That’ll do.

551
00:46:03,915 --> 00:46:09,002
Once upon a time, a demon pretended
to love a princess, kidnapped her...

552
00:46:09,082 --> 00:46:10,826
and made her his slave.

553
00:46:11,129 --> 00:46:13,001
Once she understood the betrayal,

554
00:46:13,331 --> 00:46:15,795
she made several attempts to escape.

555
00:46:16,851 --> 00:46:18,195
But she couldn’t.

556
00:46:18,275 --> 00:46:19,987
Slowly…

557
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:21,739
with no other way out…

558
00:46:21,820 --> 00:46:25,595
she began living as his obedient slave.

559
00:46:28,179 --> 00:46:29,587
One day…

560
00:46:29,850 --> 00:46:32,282
she realised she was pregnant.

561
00:46:32,362 --> 00:46:35,914
From then on, all she could think about
was the child growing inside her.

562
00:46:36,921 --> 00:46:38,729
When that child grows up…

563
00:46:38,810 --> 00:46:41,594
what if he becomes a demon like him...

564
00:46:41,920 --> 00:46:44,161
or a slave like her?

565
00:46:44,241 --> 00:46:45,729
That very thought haunted her.

566
00:46:45,810 --> 00:46:48,034
The thought turned into fear...

567
00:46:49,050 --> 00:46:50,361
then anger…

568
00:46:50,690 --> 00:46:52,354
and finally, rage.

569
00:46:54,091 --> 00:46:55,723
And so, one day…

570
00:46:56,274 --> 00:46:58,146
pregnant as she was…

571
00:46:58,786 --> 00:47:01,666
she killed the demon and buried him…

572
00:47:01,875 --> 00:47:03,922
and planted a banana tree over his grave.

573
00:47:05,554 --> 00:47:07,426
She was arrested...

574
00:47:07,810 --> 00:47:10,498
and gave birth to her child in prison.

575
00:47:11,954 --> 00:47:15,134
Determined never to
surrender her child to demons...

576
00:47:16,187 --> 00:47:19,387
or let it become a slave like herself...

577
00:47:19,906 --> 00:47:22,371
she stepped out of that prison.

578
00:47:30,826 --> 00:47:32,650
Just burn that gun.

579
00:47:32,731 --> 00:47:33,826
Why?

580
00:47:34,147 --> 00:47:35,779
I don’t need it anymore.

581
00:47:35,860 --> 00:47:37,635
You’re there for me.
-No...

582
00:47:37,858 --> 00:47:39,297
I won’t be.

583
00:47:40,251 --> 00:47:41,898
I can’t just--

584
00:47:41,979 --> 00:47:42,922
No!

585
00:47:43,003 --> 00:47:44,554
I don’t want any deep attachments.

586
00:47:44,635 --> 00:47:47,578
Just treat staying here as a job.

587
00:47:48,490 --> 00:47:52,218
And if I die,
bury me right here in this yard.

588
00:47:52,491 --> 00:47:54,546
And plant a banana tree on top.

589
00:47:54,627 --> 00:47:56,058
Let no one see me!

590
00:47:56,499 --> 00:47:57,811
And then?

591
00:47:57,892 --> 00:48:01,042
Then you may live here
comfortably with your son.

592
00:48:01,123 --> 00:48:02,763
You won’t have to go anywhere.

593
00:48:02,843 --> 00:48:05,371
But don't poison me to make that happen!

594
00:48:08,650 --> 00:48:10,346
There’s one more thing...

595
00:48:10,426 --> 00:48:12,250
I should tell you.

596
00:48:15,363 --> 00:48:16,834
What is it?

597
00:48:17,097 --> 00:48:19,770
Half my stories were just cooked up!

598
00:48:29,251 --> 00:48:30,131
Mom...

599
00:48:31,027 --> 00:48:33,923
So, my name will be Vasudev for a while?

600
00:48:34,707 --> 00:48:35,539
Yes.

601
00:48:38,115 --> 00:48:40,659
So… no more new stories to learn?

602
00:48:42,299 --> 00:48:44,459
Just learn what they teach at school.

603
00:48:44,540 --> 00:48:45,053
Okay.

604
00:48:54,932 --> 00:48:57,188
Try this. It'll look good on you.

605
00:49:06,168 --> 00:49:07,249
Nice!

606
00:49:10,299 --> 00:49:12,603
Brother, do you have perfume?

607
00:49:12,797 --> 00:49:14,909
I’ll be right back. Keep trying these on.

608
00:49:30,972 --> 00:49:32,188
Hey, dear!

609
00:49:32,860 --> 00:49:33,691
Hey!

610
00:49:36,883 --> 00:49:38,820
Where have you been all this time?

611
00:49:38,900 --> 00:49:40,483
Not a word from you!

612
00:49:44,596 --> 00:49:46,981
Look at you,
you've become so pretty!

613
00:49:48,835 --> 00:49:49,996
Wait a minute.

614
00:49:50,116 --> 00:49:52,452
It’s been three months since I got out.

615
00:49:52,532 --> 00:49:53,964
Why didn’t you call me?

616
00:49:54,300 --> 00:49:56,316
I gave you my number, right?

617
00:49:56,556 --> 00:49:57,723
You missed it?

618
00:49:59,477 --> 00:50:00,212
Well,

619
00:50:00,293 --> 00:50:01,493
where’s your kid?

620
00:50:01,844 --> 00:50:02,724
Hey!

621
00:50:02,804 --> 00:50:04,003
Make it fast!

622
00:50:05,140 --> 00:50:06,595
Those are our girls.

623
00:50:07,572 --> 00:50:10,147
I'm glad I ran into you.

624
00:50:10,291 --> 00:50:12,067
Where are you staying now?

625
00:50:14,580 --> 00:50:15,876
They’re all just trash!

626
00:50:16,419 --> 00:50:17,923
You should get in the game, dear.

627
00:50:18,276 --> 00:50:19,763
Come on, we could prosper!

628
00:50:20,187 --> 00:50:23,562
Don’t you know how much
'Shamnatha' struggled for you?

629
00:50:24,901 --> 00:50:26,692
Anyway, let me take a photo of you.

630
00:50:26,773 --> 00:50:28,100
Might come in handy.

631
00:50:29,484 --> 00:50:30,396
Hey!

632
00:50:31,339 --> 00:50:32,923
Are you leaving?

633
00:50:33,004 --> 00:50:33,931
Hey!

634
00:50:34,012 --> 00:50:35,836
What? Are you trying to avoid me!?

635
00:50:35,917 --> 00:50:37,060
Hey, stop!

636
00:50:40,673 --> 00:50:41,681
Hey!

637
00:50:41,762 --> 00:50:43,970
I’ll deal with you later!

638
00:51:03,300 --> 00:51:04,260
Stop staring…

639
00:51:04,340 --> 00:51:05,748
and go get your things.

640
00:51:06,900 --> 00:51:08,036
Go!

641
00:51:09,652 --> 00:51:11,587
I want to go to school.

642
00:51:12,827 --> 00:51:14,379
To hell with his school!

643
00:51:14,707 --> 00:51:15,804
Didn’t I tell you?

644
00:51:15,884 --> 00:51:16,652
Huh?

645
00:51:16,733 --> 00:51:19,437
When I say we can’t stay here anymore,
that’s the final word.

646
00:51:20,500 --> 00:51:22,195
You know the situation, don’t you?

647
00:51:22,435 --> 00:51:23,827
Go change your clothes.

648
00:51:25,939 --> 00:51:29,203
I said I want to go to school!

649
00:51:29,284 --> 00:51:30,468
Hey!

650
00:51:30,548 --> 00:51:32,821
You’d better go change your clothes!
Got that!?

651
00:51:32,965 --> 00:51:35,164
Or I’ll dump you here and walk away!

652
00:52:17,250 --> 00:52:18,195
Here…

653
00:52:22,692 --> 00:52:24,212
What happened?

654
00:52:25,370 --> 00:52:29,450
Didn’t I tell you...
not to leave this place?

655
00:52:34,363 --> 00:52:35,955
How long will you keep running?

656
00:52:36,036 --> 00:52:37,947
Doesn't this have to end?

657
00:52:38,028 --> 00:52:40,780
At least now, think about him.

658
00:52:40,980 --> 00:52:42,691
Live for him.

659
00:52:43,858 --> 00:52:46,626
Take this as the last
words of this old woman…

660
00:52:46,707 --> 00:52:47,730
and abide by it.

661
00:53:04,130 --> 00:53:05,362
Grandma…

662
00:53:08,243 --> 00:53:09,603
Grandma!

663
00:53:10,034 --> 00:53:11,795
Grandma!

664
00:53:17,369 --> 00:53:18,186
Grandma…

665
00:54:04,547 --> 00:54:09,506
♪ Up in the sky lives a Grandma,
our dear moon Grandma ♪

666
00:54:09,587 --> 00:54:14,091
♪ Up in the sky lives a Grandma,
our dear moon Grandma ♪

667
00:54:14,172 --> 00:54:18,684
♪ If Grandma cries,
won’t the sky cry too? ♪

668
00:54:18,764 --> 00:54:23,412
♪ If Grandma cries,
won’t the sky cry too? ♪

669
00:54:23,492 --> 00:54:28,140
♪ When Grandma smiles,
the sky blooms with moonlight ♪

670
00:54:28,220 --> 00:54:33,109
♪ When Grandma smiles,
the sky blooms with moonlight ♪

671
00:54:33,309 --> 00:54:38,238
♪ If Grandma cries,
won’t the sky cry too? ♪

672
00:54:38,948 --> 00:54:40,276
You’re quite smart.

673
00:54:40,357 --> 00:54:43,221
First time someone’s managed
to put up with Mom this long.

674
00:54:43,540 --> 00:54:44,389
Good job!

675
00:54:45,051 --> 00:54:47,451
Aha, sounds like she’s
right there with you.

676
00:54:48,036 --> 00:54:48,772
Yeah.

677
00:54:49,068 --> 00:54:52,284
Anyway, you just tell her we won't
be coming down for Christmas.

678
00:54:52,915 --> 00:54:54,091
I’ll call you next month.

679
00:54:54,172 --> 00:54:55,684
Quick! Quick!

680
00:55:17,500 --> 00:55:18,412
[gunfire]

681
00:55:19,483 --> 00:55:21,468
That grandma’s coming!

682
00:55:21,747 --> 00:55:22,835
Run!

683
00:55:23,042 --> 00:55:24,689
Hey, hurry up!

684
00:55:56,772 --> 00:55:57,859
[humming]

685
00:56:59,075 --> 00:57:00,402
[phone rings]

686
00:57:30,860 --> 00:57:31,981
Hello?

687
00:57:34,723 --> 00:57:36,052
Hello?

688
00:57:53,556 --> 00:57:54,612
[calling bell rings]

689
00:58:01,123 --> 00:58:02,212
My dear…

690
00:58:02,293 --> 00:58:03,355
Open the door.

691
00:58:03,499 --> 00:58:05,515
Look, Shamnatha is here!

692
00:58:07,531 --> 00:58:09,588
I know you’re in there.

693
00:58:11,436 --> 00:58:14,076
You can keep it shut as long as you want…

694
00:58:14,156 --> 00:58:16,300
but, Shamnatha’s not going anywhere.

695
00:58:21,476 --> 00:58:23,156
Open the door, dear.

696
00:58:23,756 --> 00:58:24,908
Hey, dear…

697
00:58:26,460 --> 00:58:27,564
Dear…

698
00:58:34,364 --> 00:58:36,444
How heartless can you be!?

699
00:58:36,524 --> 00:58:37,212
Huh?

700
00:58:37,779 --> 00:58:41,795
In jail, 'Shamnatha' protected you
like a mother hen guards her chick.

701
00:58:41,875 --> 00:58:42,491
Right!?

702
00:58:46,460 --> 00:58:48,796
And now that you’ve landed a good setup…

703
00:58:48,877 --> 00:58:50,500
Shamnatha’s just trash to you!

704
00:58:50,581 --> 00:58:52,292
-Right?
-It’s not like that…

705
00:58:52,373 --> 00:58:53,716
Yeah, yeah!

706
00:58:55,332 --> 00:58:57,700
Anyway, looks like you’re
making the right moves now.

707
00:58:57,781 --> 00:58:58,580
Well done!

708
00:58:59,907 --> 00:59:02,819
Quite a setup you’ve got here! Wow!

709
00:59:06,733 --> 00:59:08,044
Where is she?

710
00:59:08,317 --> 00:59:09,484
Where?

711
00:59:09,565 --> 00:59:10,828
Wh... Who?

712
00:59:10,909 --> 00:59:12,940
I heard there’s an old woman here.

713
00:59:13,021 --> 00:59:14,116
That…

714
00:59:14,197 --> 00:59:15,652
she’s… in the hospital.

715
00:59:17,492 --> 00:59:18,676
You killed her?

716
00:59:18,757 --> 00:59:19,860
No… no.

717
00:59:20,260 --> 00:59:22,836
What, chopped her up
and buried her somewhere!?

718
00:59:23,539 --> 00:59:25,507
That’s your signature style, huh!?

719
00:59:25,588 --> 00:59:27,411
No… I didn’t... kill her.

720
00:59:27,828 --> 00:59:29,428
Forget all that.

721
00:59:29,509 --> 00:59:31,756
Why did you run off
when you saw me that day?

722
00:59:32,323 --> 00:59:33,043
Hmm?

723
00:59:33,124 --> 00:59:35,076
I… I had to buy…

724
00:59:42,844 --> 00:59:44,412
Now, leave all that behind.

725
00:59:44,492 --> 00:59:46,604
No more suffering for you.

726
00:59:46,685 --> 00:59:49,420
Life's about to change for us, girl.

727
00:59:49,501 --> 00:59:51,244
Shamnatha’s here, right?

728
00:59:53,403 --> 00:59:54,603
Listen, dear…

729
00:59:54,684 --> 00:59:57,084
I’ve got two naive girls with me.

730
00:59:57,164 --> 00:59:58,812
I’m going to let them stay here.

731
00:59:59,107 --> 01:00:00,973
You saw them at the
shop that day, remember?

732
01:00:01,053 --> 01:00:01,765
Those girls.

733
01:00:01,845 --> 01:00:03,301
Poor things.

734
01:00:03,812 --> 01:00:04,428
Ugh!

735
01:00:04,508 --> 01:00:08,540
These policemen are such a nuisance, dear.

736
01:00:10,788 --> 01:00:12,868
But here, it’s safe.

737
01:00:13,890 --> 01:00:16,274
And you’re here too.

738
01:00:16,355 --> 01:00:18,851
You know, people are lining up out there!

739
01:00:19,507 --> 01:00:22,803
Let me call those girls and
tell them how to get here.

740
01:00:46,836 --> 01:00:48,835
Where’s your son?

741
01:00:50,388 --> 01:00:51,715
At school.

742
01:00:52,299 --> 01:00:52,938
Oh, wow…

743
01:00:53,115 --> 01:00:55,482
He’s started going to school?

744
01:01:01,539 --> 01:01:04,611
Seems you didn't like
Shamnatha coming here.

745
01:01:05,596 --> 01:01:07,580
No… nothing like that.

746
01:01:08,795 --> 01:01:10,891
Like it or not,

747
01:01:10,972 --> 01:01:13,243
Shamnatha’s here to stay!

748
01:01:16,093 --> 01:01:17,180
Tea?

749
01:01:22,661 --> 01:01:23,285
[scoffs]

750
01:01:46,476 --> 01:01:47,356
Hello?

751
01:01:47,437 --> 01:01:48,492
Have you arrived?

752
01:01:49,500 --> 01:01:52,060
Cheruthoni? Damn it, not Cheruthoni!

753
01:01:52,283 --> 01:01:54,939
It’s Cherukunnu, not Cheruthoni!

754
01:01:55,132 --> 01:01:56,211
Yeah!

755
01:01:56,772 --> 01:01:57,828
You--

756
01:01:57,908 --> 01:01:58,740
Hello?

757
01:01:58,820 --> 01:02:00,252
Call me once you--

758
01:02:00,332 --> 01:02:01,323
Ugh!

759
01:02:01,916 --> 01:02:03,260
No signal!?

760
01:02:19,700 --> 01:02:21,876
Vasudev, very good!

761
01:02:22,564 --> 01:02:24,116
See, students…

762
01:02:24,396 --> 01:02:26,092
This is how you do a project.

763
01:02:26,173 --> 01:02:28,348
Everyone, give Vasudev
a big round of applause.

764
01:02:55,932 --> 01:02:58,003
[phone ringing]

765
01:03:06,533 --> 01:03:07,176
Hello?

766
01:03:07,260 --> 01:03:09,132
How many times did I call you?

767
01:03:09,212 --> 01:03:10,236
Where were you?

768
01:03:10,316 --> 01:03:11,412
Phone not working?

769
01:03:12,236 --> 01:03:14,317
I... was at the market...

770
01:03:14,579 --> 01:03:17,204
Sir’s son and wife are
coming to Kerala today.

771
01:03:17,343 --> 01:03:19,850
Don’t tell grandma.
It’s meant to be a surprise.

772
01:03:19,934 --> 01:03:21,566
Just giving you a heads-up.

773
01:03:21,650 --> 01:03:23,225
And keep the house clean.

774
01:03:24,076 --> 01:03:25,263
When will they arrive?

775
01:03:25,347 --> 01:03:27,536
They’re almost here.
I’m waiting at the junction.

776
01:03:30,040 --> 01:03:31,173
Alright then.

777
01:03:36,212 --> 01:03:38,837
Vasudev! Vasudev!

778
01:03:39,063 --> 01:03:40,774
Vasudev, your pencil.

779
01:03:40,858 --> 01:03:42,378
You left this behind?

780
01:03:44,372 --> 01:03:45,428
Friends?

781
01:04:12,133 --> 01:04:13,156
No…

782
01:04:13,732 --> 01:04:14,773
not like that.

783
01:04:24,187 --> 01:04:26,812
Bye, Vasudev. See you tomorrow.

784
01:05:02,103 --> 01:05:03,319
[gunfire]

785
01:05:27,628 --> 01:05:29,724
From now on, however late I may be...

786
01:05:29,804 --> 01:05:31,788
leave not this place.

787
01:05:32,788 --> 01:05:34,276
Remain here.

788
01:05:35,647 --> 01:05:36,748
Mother will come!

789
01:05:54,429 --> 01:05:58,092
-Which cop harmed you?
-Pavithran, sir.

790
01:06:00,452 --> 01:06:01,796
What did he do?

791
01:06:01,877 --> 01:06:03,924
He was taking revenge on my son, sir.

792
01:06:04,005 --> 01:06:05,829
He ran him over with a vehicle
and put him in the hospital.

793
01:06:05,910 --> 01:06:07,358
Hold on, he ran him over?

794
01:06:07,439 --> 01:06:09,670
If that was intentional,
that’s attempted murder.

795
01:06:09,751 --> 01:06:10,543
Didn’t you file a case?

796
01:06:10,623 --> 01:06:13,255
He didn’t do it himself, sir.
He used another lorry driver.

797
01:06:13,373 --> 01:06:14,909
Then how are you sure it was Pavithran?

798
01:06:14,989 --> 01:06:16,141
The next day,

799
01:06:16,222 --> 01:06:19,245
he came to my house
for passport verification.

800
01:06:19,326 --> 01:06:22,373
He returned the form stating
that my son wasn't at home.

801
01:06:22,453 --> 01:06:24,613
Wait, what’s his problem with your son?

802
01:06:24,694 --> 01:06:28,260
They had some scuffle ages ago
while playing on the ground.

803
01:06:28,811 --> 01:06:31,451
Since then, he hasn’t let
my son live in peace, sir.

804
01:06:31,996 --> 01:06:35,236
My son had just secured a job
and was about to leave for the Gulf.

805
01:06:35,316 --> 01:06:36,869
-That’s when this happened.
-Hey…

806
01:06:36,949 --> 01:06:38,726
Just because of a silly playground fight,

807
01:06:38,807 --> 01:06:41,030
you're saying he tried to kill him?

808
01:06:41,738 --> 01:06:43,729
Your son was probably
hit by some random lorry.

809
01:06:43,810 --> 01:06:45,074
Don’t jump to conclusions.

810
01:06:45,155 --> 01:06:46,366
No, sir.

811
01:06:46,643 --> 01:06:48,490
I’m sure it was him.

812
01:06:50,187 --> 01:06:51,178
Given Pavithran,

813
01:06:51,258 --> 01:06:53,179
there's a chance something
like that could've happened, sir.

814
01:06:53,260 --> 01:06:54,923
He’s a strange fellow!

815
01:06:59,772 --> 01:07:00,796
Pavithran…

816
01:07:01,179 --> 01:07:02,603
Sir is calling you.

817
01:07:07,918 --> 01:07:08,670
Sir!

818
01:07:09,590 --> 01:07:10,502
Uncle?

819
01:07:10,583 --> 01:07:11,718
What brings you here?

820
01:07:14,430 --> 01:07:17,613
Why are you taking revenge
over such petty matters?

821
01:07:18,117 --> 01:07:20,253
Revenge? Sir, he’s my relative.

822
01:07:20,334 --> 01:07:21,516
Why would I do that?

823
01:07:21,597 --> 01:07:23,317
You run over anyone
you have a grudge against?

824
01:07:23,398 --> 01:07:24,437
Shall I file a case?

825
01:07:24,549 --> 01:07:26,742
Sir, that’s a case I investigated myself.

826
01:07:26,822 --> 01:07:29,261
If you investigate it
too and find me guilty,

827
01:07:29,341 --> 01:07:30,414
you may punish me.

828
01:07:30,494 --> 01:07:33,374
Why didn’t you clear his
son’s passport verification?

829
01:07:33,606 --> 01:07:35,605
Sir, I went to his house for verification…

830
01:07:35,686 --> 01:07:36,742
-He wasn’t there--
-Hey!

831
01:07:36,823 --> 01:07:40,279
I’ve dealt with plenty of smart crooks
like you to reach this chair!

832
01:07:40,359 --> 01:07:41,655
Got that?

833
01:07:41,736 --> 01:07:44,520
You’d better clear his son’s verification!

834
01:07:44,601 --> 01:07:46,825
Oh no, sir… I’ve already sent it back.

835
01:07:47,893 --> 01:07:50,310
You… you step outside. Get out!

836
01:07:50,390 --> 01:07:51,949
Your duty isn’t over. I’ll call you.

837
01:07:52,030 --> 01:07:52,782
-Go.
-Sir!

838
01:07:53,796 --> 01:07:54,821
Uncle…

839
01:07:56,757 --> 01:07:59,046
You can go. I’ll get it cleared.

840
01:08:01,605 --> 01:08:03,717
Go! He won't harm you.

841
01:08:15,780 --> 01:08:17,844
Don't let him go.
Keep him buried in some case.

842
01:08:17,925 --> 01:08:18,557
Sir!

843
01:08:27,060 --> 01:08:28,469
Ugh, what a stink!

844
01:08:28,549 --> 01:08:29,779
Should I quit smoking?

845
01:08:29,861 --> 01:08:31,163
No need for that.

846
01:08:31,245 --> 01:08:33,524
Just brush your teeth
before you try to kiss me.

847
01:08:34,243 --> 01:08:35,693
Then I have a suggestion.

848
01:08:35,773 --> 01:08:37,380
Can you come home this evening?

849
01:08:37,461 --> 01:08:39,487
I'll brush up and make
up for it with a few kisses.

850
01:08:39,631 --> 01:08:40,916
What excuse am I supposed to give at home?

851
01:08:40,997 --> 01:08:43,292
Tell them it’s extra duty.
They won’t question it.

852
01:08:43,372 --> 01:08:45,941
It’s not like they don’t know about us.

853
01:08:46,020 --> 01:08:47,501
But that’s only after marriage.

854
01:08:47,581 --> 01:08:48,587
Damn the marriage!

855
01:08:49,037 --> 01:08:50,124
I’ll come.

856
01:08:51,892 --> 01:08:55,076
You know the SI is madly in love with you.

857
01:08:55,157 --> 01:08:57,462
And he dumps all that anger on me.

858
01:08:57,542 --> 01:08:59,023
As if it’s not because of your own antics!

859
01:08:59,103 --> 01:09:00,879
-What’s wrong with my antics?
-Pavithran…

860
01:09:01,798 --> 01:09:04,862
We got a call. A boy's been
standing by the road for hours.

861
01:09:05,124 --> 01:09:06,292
You go check it.

862
01:09:06,765 --> 01:09:08,243
Can I go home after that, sir?

863
01:09:08,323 --> 01:09:10,300
Report back here first,
then you can leave.

864
01:09:16,884 --> 01:09:18,292
Cicily, dear...

865
01:09:18,372 --> 01:09:20,470
You need to be careful with Pavithran.

866
01:09:20,551 --> 01:09:22,734
He wouldn’t hesitate to harm someone.

867
01:09:23,124 --> 01:09:25,188
He only harms people he dislikes...

868
01:09:25,572 --> 01:09:27,252
but he’s very fond of me, sir.

869
01:09:46,252 --> 01:09:47,227
Who are all of you?

870
01:09:47,723 --> 01:09:48,738
-We live nearby, sir.
-Huh?

871
01:09:49,026 --> 01:09:51,202
Why is he standing here
in just his underwear?

872
01:09:52,187 --> 01:09:53,787
What’s your name, son?

873
01:09:53,939 --> 01:09:54,851
Who are you?

874
01:09:54,932 --> 01:09:56,299
Sir, I’m the one who called you.

875
01:09:56,380 --> 01:09:58,082
Has he been standing
half-naked all this time?

876
01:09:58,163 --> 01:09:59,827
No, sir. He had his uniform and schoolbag.

877
01:09:59,908 --> 01:10:00,795
Then where's it?

878
01:10:00,875 --> 01:10:02,107
I stepped away to buy a cigarette.

879
01:10:02,188 --> 01:10:03,987
So I didn’t see what happened then.

880
01:10:08,860 --> 01:10:09,836
Boy...

881
01:10:10,171 --> 01:10:12,187
Who took off your clothes?

882
01:10:12,691 --> 01:10:13,699
Huh?

883
01:10:14,324 --> 01:10:15,908
What’s your name?

884
01:10:17,196 --> 01:10:18,179
Say something!

885
01:10:18,260 --> 01:10:19,908
I tried too, sir…
but he didn’t say anything.

886
01:10:26,130 --> 01:10:28,179
Where the hell did you pop up from!?

887
01:10:34,147 --> 01:10:36,115
Why doesn’t he have any clothes on?

888
01:10:36,196 --> 01:10:37,540
That’s how I found him, sir.

889
01:10:37,620 --> 01:10:39,556
Why didn’t you get him some clothes?

890
01:10:40,955 --> 01:10:42,268
Do one thing...

891
01:10:42,348 --> 01:10:46,211
Buy him some clothes, ask around
again and get him back home.

892
01:10:46,292 --> 01:10:48,196
Sir, how am I supposed to manage that?

893
01:10:48,276 --> 01:10:50,195
He won’t even say a word.

894
01:10:55,540 --> 01:10:56,596
Sir...

895
01:10:56,850 --> 01:10:57,938
anyway...

896
01:10:58,019 --> 01:11:01,427
someone will come by morning
saying the boy’s missing, right?

897
01:11:01,507 --> 01:11:03,731
So, why don’t we deal
with the rest tomorrow?

898
01:11:05,164 --> 01:11:06,539
Yeah, that’ll do.

899
01:11:06,932 --> 01:11:09,364
Anyway, let him stay with you tonight!

900
01:11:10,083 --> 01:11:11,251
Sir…

901
01:11:42,276 --> 01:11:42,852
Come.

902
01:11:45,173 --> 01:11:45,797
He slept.

903
01:11:46,414 --> 01:11:47,470
Got everything?

904
01:13:09,740 --> 01:13:10,476
Hey!

905
01:13:11,700 --> 01:13:13,188
When you saw him…

906
01:13:13,269 --> 01:13:15,396
-Are you sure he was in uniform?
-Yes, sir.

907
01:13:15,477 --> 01:13:16,917
Do you remember which school?

908
01:13:16,998 --> 01:13:18,909
That's not easy.
A lot of school buses pass this way.

909
01:13:18,990 --> 01:13:19,980
You know that, sir.

910
01:13:23,636 --> 01:13:26,324
Who took your uniform off, kid!?

911
01:13:27,548 --> 01:13:28,380
Hey!

912
01:14:06,404 --> 01:14:09,284
Still, who took it off him
and threw it here?

913
01:14:09,477 --> 01:14:11,260
No one else...

914
01:14:11,340 --> 01:14:12,796
he did it himself!

915
01:14:16,892 --> 01:14:18,365
Vasudev!

916
01:14:19,349 --> 01:14:21,924
Why are you in this dress?
Aren’t you coming?

917
01:14:28,164 --> 01:14:29,172
Hey, hey!

918
01:14:32,020 --> 01:14:33,299
Stop right there!

919
01:14:34,773 --> 01:14:36,420
What nonsense are you talking?

920
01:14:36,501 --> 01:14:38,789
If needed, run his photo in the newspaper.

921
01:14:39,253 --> 01:14:40,884
His parents will see it
and come looking for him.

922
01:14:40,965 --> 01:14:42,717
This doesn’t need a big investigation!

923
01:14:42,798 --> 01:14:44,717
That’s not it, sir… something feels wrong.

924
01:14:44,797 --> 01:14:46,668
He doesn’t seem like an ordinary kid.

925
01:14:46,749 --> 01:14:48,492
As if he’s some terrorist!

926
01:14:49,421 --> 01:14:51,773
Sir, I got his school details.

927
01:14:51,853 --> 01:14:53,772
Sir, give me a day.
Let me look into it.

928
01:14:53,853 --> 01:14:55,700
Just because you took the SI test,

929
01:14:55,781 --> 01:14:57,309
don’t act like some big-shot CID!

930
01:14:57,405 --> 01:14:59,206
Go to the school and get his address.

931
01:14:59,287 --> 01:15:01,901
Trace it and find someone
responsible for him!

932
01:15:01,981 --> 01:15:02,756
Simple as that.

933
01:15:02,837 --> 01:15:03,557
Understood?

934
01:15:04,027 --> 01:15:04,891
Sir!

935
01:15:09,532 --> 01:15:11,963
Hey, I need to step out for a bit.
Can you watch him?

936
01:15:13,099 --> 01:15:14,363
Seriously?

937
01:15:14,443 --> 01:15:15,652
Don't make it a big deal.

938
01:15:15,732 --> 01:15:17,380
I know how to handle a kid.

939
01:15:17,460 --> 01:15:18,692
Then I’ll be off.

940
01:15:18,773 --> 01:15:19,571
Yeah!

941
01:15:44,789 --> 01:15:45,893
Yes, Gopi sir?

942
01:15:46,349 --> 01:15:48,044
I’ll send you an address.

943
01:15:48,125 --> 01:15:50,060
It falls under your station limits.

944
01:15:50,141 --> 01:15:51,836
Can you get me the details?

945
01:15:52,452 --> 01:15:53,844
It’s a bit urgent.

946
01:16:10,995 --> 01:16:12,595
The address is correct, sir...

947
01:16:12,676 --> 01:16:14,071
but everything else seems wrong.

948
01:16:14,587 --> 01:16:16,987
No such house or family exists here.

949
01:16:18,899 --> 01:16:21,475
Have you… seen this boy anywhere?

950
01:16:22,715 --> 01:16:24,443
No, not around here, sir.

951
01:16:27,044 --> 01:16:27,971
Alright.

952
01:16:39,748 --> 01:16:40,884
Yes, Gopi sir?

953
01:16:40,965 --> 01:16:44,318
Pavithran, I checked the address you gave.

954
01:16:44,693 --> 01:16:47,668
That Girija and her husband
are settled in Dubai now.

955
01:16:47,748 --> 01:16:50,483
And that boy named
Vasudev is no longer alive.

956
01:16:50,564 --> 01:16:51,284
What?

957
01:16:52,030 --> 01:16:55,130
There was a school rickshaw accident
a few months ago.

958
01:16:55,214 --> 01:16:57,038
He was one of three kids who died.

959
01:17:02,795 --> 01:17:04,396
Got you!

960
01:17:09,731 --> 01:17:11,011
Yes, Sabu sir?

961
01:17:11,731 --> 01:17:13,492
Sir, things aren't adding up here.

962
01:17:14,131 --> 01:17:16,579
The name we got from the
school doesn’t match him.

963
01:17:16,825 --> 01:17:20,393
The boy with that name died in
an accident a few months ago.

964
01:17:20,477 --> 01:17:21,876
What are you talking about?

965
01:17:21,957 --> 01:17:23,252
It must be a clerical error.

966
01:17:23,333 --> 01:17:24,172
Sir… but--

967
01:17:24,252 --> 01:17:26,198
We need to investigate this thoroughly.

968
01:17:26,387 --> 01:17:28,291
Francis sir won’t listen if I tell him.

969
01:17:28,372 --> 01:17:32,308
Right now, we’re tied up with an
inquest on the cooperative bank robbery.

970
01:17:32,612 --> 01:17:35,284
I also checked with
the East Police Station.

971
01:17:35,460 --> 01:17:37,403
No missing complaint
has been reported there.

972
01:17:37,484 --> 01:17:39,428
You just get back here
as soon as possible.

973
01:17:57,797 --> 01:17:59,076
Stop playing!

974
01:17:59,157 --> 01:18:00,149
Go sit there!

975
01:18:03,196 --> 01:18:04,636
Have you seen this boy?

976
01:18:04,716 --> 01:18:07,341
Yes… I had seen him walking that way.

977
01:18:07,422 --> 01:18:08,405
This way?

978
01:18:17,159 --> 01:18:18,998
-Pavithran!
-Oh, hey…

979
01:18:19,445 --> 01:18:20,647
What are you doing here?

980
01:18:20,727 --> 01:18:22,159
I came here on another case.

981
01:18:22,463 --> 01:18:23,599
What's going on?

982
01:18:24,191 --> 01:18:26,143
You didn't hear? It’s a murder.

983
01:18:26,335 --> 01:18:27,503
Not one, but two.

984
01:18:27,695 --> 01:18:29,807
The maid who worked here did it.

985
01:18:35,900 --> 01:18:36,975
That’s serious trouble.

986
01:18:37,056 --> 01:18:37,983
Of course!

987
01:18:38,519 --> 01:18:40,247
-We've got a problem too.
-What?

988
01:18:40,328 --> 01:18:42,207
Robbery at the cooperative bank.

989
01:18:43,421 --> 01:18:47,420
Also, was that maid here alone?
Did she have a child?

990
01:18:47,501 --> 01:18:48,476
Anyone else with her?

991
01:18:48,716 --> 01:18:49,895
No… no kids.

992
01:18:50,184 --> 01:18:52,751
If there were, we’d have found
their clothes or something.

993
01:18:52,832 --> 01:18:55,487
All we found were
some of the woman’s clothes.

994
01:18:56,463 --> 01:18:57,903
Why did you ask?

995
01:18:57,984 --> 01:18:59,184
No… nothing.

996
01:19:01,495 --> 01:19:03,271
Hey, isn't that boy there?

997
01:19:03,543 --> 01:19:05,432
Yeah, he was around here.

998
01:19:05,512 --> 01:19:07,208
He was? Go check!

999
01:19:07,791 --> 01:19:09,727
Why the hell did I leave him with you?

1000
01:19:15,166 --> 01:19:17,407
Sister… did you see that boy?

1001
01:19:17,487 --> 01:19:18,326
No, I didn’t.

1002
01:19:22,079 --> 01:19:24,302
-What’s wrong?
-No, nothing.

1003
01:20:07,863 --> 01:20:09,175
Sir, that boy is missing.

1004
01:20:09,255 --> 01:20:10,007
I know that!

1005
01:20:10,287 --> 01:20:12,207
That’s exactly why I rushed down here!

1006
01:20:12,470 --> 01:20:15,030
Sir, how about we publish
his photo in the newspaper?

1007
01:20:15,110 --> 01:20:16,854
Didn’t I say that first, damn it!?

1008
01:20:16,934 --> 01:20:19,358
But you had to act smart
and play Sherlock Holmes!

1009
01:20:20,120 --> 01:20:22,247
I even informed Childline.

1010
01:20:22,328 --> 01:20:25,719
That boy could be an eyewitness or
even the culprit in the murder case.

1011
01:20:27,167 --> 01:20:28,783
I’ll make sure you get fired!

1012
01:20:28,863 --> 01:20:30,911
But he didn’t go missing from me, sir.

1013
01:20:40,367 --> 01:20:41,663
Pavithran…

1014
01:20:41,744 --> 01:20:44,471
You do realise the consequences
of what you just said, right?

1015
01:20:44,727 --> 01:20:46,989
And how it will affect Cicily?

1016
01:20:47,222 --> 01:20:48,678
Brother Soman, come.

1017
01:20:49,287 --> 01:20:50,184
Sir…

1018
01:20:50,265 --> 01:20:51,239
I’ll investigate this case.

1019
01:20:51,320 --> 01:20:52,536
Enough of your crap!

1020
01:21:05,260 --> 01:21:06,318
Cicily…

1021
01:21:06,495 --> 01:21:07,127
I wasn’t--

1022
01:21:07,208 --> 01:21:08,918
I ignored everyone who warned me.

1023
01:21:09,503 --> 01:21:11,663
But you’ve just shown your true colours.

1024
01:21:20,902 --> 01:21:23,382
Dear, calm down. Let’s do the needful.

1025
01:21:23,462 --> 01:21:24,478
You go now.

1026
01:22:50,374 --> 01:22:51,158
Stop the bus.

1027
01:22:51,239 --> 01:22:51,775
[In Tulu] What’s wrong?

1028
01:22:52,016 --> 01:22:53,599
Just let Abba know. I'm getting down here.

1029
01:22:55,064 --> 01:22:56,088
Should I come with you?

1030
01:22:56,243 --> 01:22:57,104
No, no.

1031
01:22:57,184 --> 01:22:58,240
I’ll call you.

1032
01:24:23,414 --> 01:24:25,958
♪ Have you seen the key? ♪

1033
01:24:26,039 --> 01:24:28,830
♪ The tiny froggy's key ♪

1034
01:24:28,910 --> 01:24:33,950
♪ The key that slipped away
while wandering here and there ♪

1035
01:24:34,031 --> 01:24:37,310
♪ The key that slipped away ♪

1036
01:25:49,330 --> 01:25:50,307
Bro...

1037
01:25:50,946 --> 01:25:52,306
Why’s that house locked up?

1038
01:25:52,387 --> 01:25:53,914
No one lives there anymore.

1039
01:25:53,995 --> 01:25:54,834
What happened?

1040
01:25:55,098 --> 01:25:56,250
Who are you?

1041
01:25:56,691 --> 01:25:58,626
My uncle runs a coffee business.

1042
01:25:58,707 --> 01:26:00,730
I came to check if they
had any coffee beans to sell.

1043
01:26:01,218 --> 01:26:02,691
How can I contact them?

1044
01:26:02,771 --> 01:26:04,794
There’s no one left
alive there to contact.

1045
01:26:04,875 --> 01:26:06,778
Only a crazy old grandma lived there.

1046
01:26:06,859 --> 01:26:08,906
And she was murdered by her home nurse.

1047
01:26:13,698 --> 01:26:14,626
Why?

1048
01:26:14,707 --> 01:26:16,114
Maybe she caught her stealing.

1049
01:26:16,195 --> 01:26:18,802
On top of that, she even shot
the family who came looking for her.

1050
01:26:23,802 --> 01:26:25,002
And then?

1051
01:26:25,083 --> 01:26:26,043
What happened to the nurse?

1052
01:26:26,123 --> 01:26:27,810
The police caught her the same day.

1053
01:26:27,891 --> 01:26:30,003
That was actually
the first time we saw her.

1054
01:26:30,083 --> 01:26:31,294
What a crowd it was!

1055
01:26:31,375 --> 01:26:32,052
Yeah!

1056
01:26:32,133 --> 01:26:33,902
Never before had such
a crowd gathered here.

1057
01:27:02,566 --> 01:27:03,655
Sir...

1058
01:27:05,662 --> 01:27:06,559
Sir...

1059
01:27:06,847 --> 01:27:09,439
A lady police officer
was working here, right?

1060
01:27:09,519 --> 01:27:10,663
A lady officer?

1061
01:27:11,119 --> 01:27:12,646
There are many lady officers here.

1062
01:27:12,727 --> 01:27:13,734
Who are you looking for?

1063
01:27:15,975 --> 01:27:18,599
She worked here about 6-7 years ago.

1064
01:27:18,680 --> 01:27:20,768
I think her name was Cicily.

1065
01:27:20,848 --> 01:27:22,678
It's only been 2 years since I came here.

1066
01:27:22,814 --> 01:27:24,118
Tell me what this is about.

1067
01:27:26,558 --> 01:27:28,990
Is anyone from that time still here?

1068
01:27:29,071 --> 01:27:30,254
Just tell me what the matter is.

1069
01:27:31,831 --> 01:27:32,998
I mean...

1070
01:27:34,614 --> 01:27:37,062
What is it, man?
I’m the one taking all the flak!

1071
01:27:39,271 --> 01:27:40,967
Sir, wait a minute.

1072
01:27:45,502 --> 01:27:46,399
Sir...

1073
01:27:47,111 --> 01:27:48,007
Yes, tell me.

1074
01:27:48,087 --> 01:27:49,478
Do you remember me, sir?

1075
01:27:50,695 --> 01:27:51,703
No, I don’t.

1076
01:27:51,783 --> 01:27:55,279
I came here once when I
was about 5-6 years old.

1077
01:27:57,462 --> 01:27:59,622
Soman, don’t go. You have duty.

1078
01:28:03,574 --> 01:28:05,014
Who’s this?

1079
01:28:05,191 --> 01:28:06,662
Just a small case.

1080
01:28:06,743 --> 01:28:08,030
No, sir...

1081
01:28:09,319 --> 01:28:11,014
Sir, don’t you recognise me?

1082
01:28:12,134 --> 01:28:14,599
I’m the one who stayed in your room...

1083
01:28:14,679 --> 01:28:15,815
many years ago.

1084
01:28:17,966 --> 01:28:19,135
Hey!

1085
01:28:19,735 --> 01:28:20,551
You?

1086
01:28:25,781 --> 01:28:26,694
What brings you here?

1087
01:28:26,774 --> 01:28:29,046
Came back to collect
something you left behind?

1088
01:28:30,126 --> 01:28:32,830
Or to finish that little
hide-and-seek from before?

1089
01:28:35,398 --> 01:28:37,366
I need a favour, sir.

1090
01:28:37,998 --> 01:28:39,166
Why not?

1091
01:28:39,294 --> 01:28:41,917
This whole station
runs just for your needs!

1092
01:28:43,245 --> 01:28:44,237
Come.

1093
01:28:46,381 --> 01:28:47,341
Come on.

1094
01:29:03,173 --> 01:29:04,133
Sir...

1095
01:29:05,229 --> 01:29:06,765
Where's that lady officer, sir?

1096
01:29:06,909 --> 01:29:08,285
Did you marry her?

1097
01:29:10,734 --> 01:29:12,190
She got married...

1098
01:29:12,885 --> 01:29:14,550
just not to me.

1099
01:29:18,941 --> 01:29:21,165
Do you know anything about my mom?

1100
01:29:21,884 --> 01:29:23,644
Where were you all this time?

1101
01:29:24,261 --> 01:29:26,454
Only now you suddenly
remembered your mother?

1102
01:29:27,910 --> 01:29:29,814
Sir, I made a mistake back then.

1103
01:29:29,894 --> 01:29:30,622
I’m sorry.

1104
01:29:32,596 --> 01:29:34,292
I was passing through just now...

1105
01:29:34,373 --> 01:29:35,908
and I recognised this place.

1106
01:29:37,278 --> 01:29:39,054
Sir, please help me.

1107
01:29:40,285 --> 01:29:42,510
I’ll listen to your story.

1108
01:29:43,062 --> 01:29:44,517
But before that...

1109
01:29:45,629 --> 01:29:46,518
do one thing.

1110
01:29:46,598 --> 01:29:48,117
Go get me some water.

1111
01:29:50,293 --> 01:29:51,733
Your mother, huh?

1112
01:29:51,814 --> 01:29:52,878
We’ll see what can be done.

1113
01:29:53,318 --> 01:29:54,518
Go get the water.

1114
01:30:14,758 --> 01:30:16,534
Why did you come here?

1115
01:30:16,918 --> 01:30:18,390
My mom...

1116
01:30:19,597 --> 01:30:21,549
He’s not going to spare you.

1117
01:30:21,630 --> 01:30:23,805
And he won’t help
you find your mother either!

1118
01:30:23,886 --> 01:30:26,166
You need to get out of here immediately.

1119
01:30:26,526 --> 01:30:28,285
I have no other option.

1120
01:30:28,550 --> 01:30:30,262
I have to find my mom.

1121
01:30:33,830 --> 01:30:35,815
I’ll give you a cop’s number.

1122
01:30:36,189 --> 01:30:37,405
His name is George.

1123
01:30:37,486 --> 01:30:39,501
Your mom’s case was handled
at the station where he works.

1124
01:30:39,582 --> 01:30:41,574
Call him and meet him once.

1125
01:30:42,462 --> 01:30:43,326
Go.

1126
01:30:44,197 --> 01:30:47,509
If you don’t leave now,
you may never get the chance again!

1127
01:30:53,022 --> 01:30:55,486
-Where is he?
-He ran away, sir.

1128
01:30:56,590 --> 01:30:58,638
You must’ve scared him off, right?

1129
01:30:58,718 --> 01:31:00,190
No, sir. I didn’t say anything.

1130
01:31:00,271 --> 01:31:01,119
Damn!

1131
01:31:01,478 --> 01:31:05,095
I had already prepared myself
to help him find his mother.

1132
01:31:07,230 --> 01:31:08,478
Soman, you may go.

1133
01:31:13,687 --> 01:31:15,654
I’ve stepped out to meet George.

1134
01:31:18,286 --> 01:31:19,693
Yeah, let's go there.

1135
01:31:21,973 --> 01:31:23,637
Listen, George...

1136
01:31:24,069 --> 01:31:25,782
Things aren’t like they used to be.

1137
01:31:25,862 --> 01:31:29,878
These days, it’s very difficult to dig
up an old file or someone’s details.

1138
01:31:31,366 --> 01:31:33,493
But I did it only because you asked.

1139
01:31:35,350 --> 01:31:37,158
Your mother is a handful.

1140
01:31:37,927 --> 01:31:40,615
She tried to escape from prison twice.

1141
01:31:43,462 --> 01:31:45,110
She injured nearly 7-8 people.

1142
01:31:45,526 --> 01:31:47,222
One of them was a lady officer.

1143
01:31:47,503 --> 01:31:49,871
She lashed out,
saying she wanted to see her son.

1144
01:31:54,014 --> 01:31:55,663
Where is my son?!

1145
01:31:56,206 --> 01:31:58,190
Where is my son?!

1146
01:31:58,711 --> 01:32:00,694
Where is my son?!

1147
01:32:02,264 --> 01:32:04,247
Since they couldn’t control her,

1148
01:32:04,567 --> 01:32:07,991
they declared her mentally unstable
and sent her to a mental hospital.

1149
01:32:08,735 --> 01:32:10,559
What a tragedy, right, George?

1150
01:32:19,462 --> 01:32:21,589
How long has it been
since you saw your mom?

1151
01:32:22,526 --> 01:32:24,878
Almost... 6-7 years.

1152
01:32:24,959 --> 01:32:26,567
Where were you all this time?

1153
01:32:26,878 --> 01:32:27,719
I...

1154
01:32:27,800 --> 01:32:28,310
Sir...

1155
01:32:28,646 --> 01:32:30,806
-Any update?
-I know this woman.

1156
01:32:30,991 --> 01:32:33,503
When they brought her in,
she was extremely violent.

1157
01:32:37,926 --> 01:32:38,982
Open it!

1158
01:32:39,062 --> 01:32:40,453
I said open it!

1159
01:32:41,190 --> 01:32:43,453
But once the medication kicked in,

1160
01:32:43,534 --> 01:32:45,502
she’d just sit quietly somewhere.

1161
01:32:46,727 --> 01:32:49,751
She was here for about two years.

1162
01:32:49,991 --> 01:32:52,039
By then, her sentence had also ended.

1163
01:32:52,119 --> 01:32:55,367
But if no one claims them,
we'll have to keep them here.

1164
01:32:55,448 --> 01:32:56,999
So… is she still here?

1165
01:32:58,327 --> 01:33:00,679
After that, she remained
here for a while longer.

1166
01:33:01,735 --> 01:33:04,375
But our records show
someone claimed her later.

1167
01:33:06,829 --> 01:33:07,726
Who?

1168
01:33:08,214 --> 01:33:10,006
My mom has no one but me.

1169
01:33:11,902 --> 01:33:13,663
It’s listed as her brother.

1170
01:33:13,871 --> 01:33:15,471
Name: Pavithran KS.

1171
01:33:42,007 --> 01:33:42,919
Hey...

1172
01:33:43,319 --> 01:33:44,327
Sir is calling you in.

1173
01:33:53,134 --> 01:33:54,446
What’s going on?

1174
01:33:54,607 --> 01:33:56,485
It’s been two days since
you went to get water!

1175
01:33:56,566 --> 01:33:58,342
Why are you holding my mom captive?

1176
01:33:58,670 --> 01:34:00,174
Your tone has changed.

1177
01:34:00,886 --> 01:34:02,950
Getting cocky because
I was friendly with you?

1178
01:34:03,031 --> 01:34:04,645
The register says you took her.

1179
01:34:05,791 --> 01:34:07,535
I’ll take whoever I want.

1180
01:34:07,783 --> 01:34:09,319
If you’ve got a complaint...

1181
01:34:09,399 --> 01:34:10,558
submit it over there.

1182
01:34:10,854 --> 01:34:12,469
And when you file it...

1183
01:34:12,550 --> 01:34:14,965
attach some proof that she’s your mother.

1184
01:34:15,559 --> 01:34:17,815
An ID card or something, okay?

1185
01:34:20,645 --> 01:34:21,701
Oh wait...

1186
01:34:22,198 --> 01:34:24,598
even your birth certificate is fake.

1187
01:34:25,221 --> 01:34:26,245
Isn’t it?

1188
01:34:30,534 --> 01:34:31,701
What will you do?

1189
01:34:32,981 --> 01:34:33,517
Sir...

1190
01:34:33,598 --> 01:34:36,093
We got a call from the forest department.
They've crossed the border.

1191
01:34:36,173 --> 01:34:37,052
Oh wait. Okay, okay.

1192
01:34:39,541 --> 01:34:40,950
Sir! Please, sir!

1193
01:34:42,510 --> 01:34:46,414
Aren’t you the one who outsmarted
all those cops and got away?

1194
01:34:47,821 --> 01:34:49,437
So, find her the official way.

1195
01:34:57,668 --> 01:34:58,484
Sir!

1196
01:34:59,861 --> 01:35:01,428
-Sir, my mom...
-Get your hands off me!

1197
01:35:05,246 --> 01:35:06,030
Didn’t I tell you?

1198
01:35:06,223 --> 01:35:07,358
Search for her your own way!

1199
01:35:07,646 --> 01:35:08,430
Let’s go!

1200
01:35:21,239 --> 01:35:23,015
Why did you come back?

1201
01:35:23,534 --> 01:35:25,054
He’s taken my mom away.

1202
01:35:28,686 --> 01:35:30,765
Sir, do you know... where my mom is?

1203
01:35:30,846 --> 01:35:32,685
I only know what happened
until she was jailed.

1204
01:35:32,766 --> 01:35:33,853
Sir...

1205
01:35:34,534 --> 01:35:36,517
Can you please help me, sir?

1206
01:35:36,598 --> 01:35:40,198
I’m trying to wrap this up and
get away from him for good.

1207
01:35:40,573 --> 01:35:42,109
Pavithran isn’t the man you take him for!

1208
01:35:42,190 --> 01:35:45,287
Even though it wasn’t intentional,
he lost Cicily because of you.

1209
01:35:45,678 --> 01:35:47,629
Before he does something
dangerous to you...

1210
01:35:47,710 --> 01:35:49,374
leave this place, son.

1211
01:36:56,485 --> 01:36:57,654
When did he come?

1212
01:36:57,734 --> 01:36:59,301
He’s been around since morning, sir.

1213
01:37:30,020 --> 01:37:32,107
Yet another serious lapse
on your station's part!

1214
01:37:32,191 --> 01:37:34,223
Sir, that was a mistake--

1215
01:37:34,307 --> 01:37:35,453
How many years has it been?

1216
01:37:35,537 --> 01:37:37,320
A new excuse every damn year!

1217
01:37:37,663 --> 01:37:39,597
If you can't handle the job,
step down, Pavithran!

1218
01:37:39,760 --> 01:37:41,985
I want the full report by Friday!

1219
01:37:42,069 --> 01:37:43,014
I'll take care of it, sir.

1220
01:37:43,094 --> 01:37:45,213
I'll... send it over soon, sir.

1221
01:38:02,815 --> 01:38:03,551
What is it?

1222
01:38:03,632 --> 01:38:05,647
-He’s becoming a real pain.
-You go inside.

1223
01:38:09,398 --> 01:38:10,423
What are you up to?

1224
01:38:10,671 --> 01:38:12,206
Is this some kind of protest?

1225
01:38:12,406 --> 01:38:13,766
Not going to say anything?

1226
01:38:13,871 --> 01:38:15,470
A protest to get your mom back?

1227
01:38:15,551 --> 01:38:17,039
Sir, what exactly do you want?

1228
01:38:17,120 --> 01:38:17,918
What?

1229
01:38:17,999 --> 01:38:19,862
What revenge are you taking
on me by holding my mom?

1230
01:38:19,943 --> 01:38:20,654
You?

1231
01:38:20,991 --> 01:38:21,999
Come here!

1232
01:38:24,678 --> 01:38:26,518
What can I possibly do to you?

1233
01:38:27,079 --> 01:38:28,759
Take your time and decide, sir.

1234
01:38:28,839 --> 01:38:30,079
I’ll be right here.

1235
01:38:32,293 --> 01:38:34,959
You’re not giving my mom back
because you lost that lady officer, right?

1236
01:38:35,040 --> 01:38:36,343
You little brat!

1237
01:38:36,423 --> 01:38:38,446
Trying to provoke me with your big talk?

1238
01:38:43,438 --> 01:38:46,558
Let’s see if your mom can survive
without her hands and legs.

1239
01:38:48,231 --> 01:38:50,022
Shall I send them to you in pieces?

1240
01:38:50,566 --> 01:38:52,039
One instalment at a time!

1241
01:38:52,263 --> 01:38:53,134
Huh?

1242
01:38:56,222 --> 01:38:58,655
Or maybe I just won’t
return your mother at all.

1243
01:38:59,863 --> 01:39:01,303
Do whatever you can!

1244
01:39:05,319 --> 01:39:06,599
This is how I deal with things!

1245
01:39:18,959 --> 01:39:20,030
Hey! Hey!

1246
01:39:20,982 --> 01:39:23,094
-Didn’t you leave?
-No. I won’t leave without my mom!

1247
01:39:23,174 --> 01:39:24,709
Can’t you understand?

1248
01:39:24,790 --> 01:39:26,790
I’ve got bigger criminals
to deal with here!

1249
01:39:26,870 --> 01:39:29,221
Just show her to me, sir.
At least I’ll know she’s alive.

1250
01:39:29,302 --> 01:39:31,350
What do I gain from doing that?

1251
01:39:31,822 --> 01:39:33,805
Get out! Come back when you’ve grown up.

1252
01:39:33,886 --> 01:39:35,310
Then I'll decide how to deal with you!

1253
01:39:35,390 --> 01:39:36,606
No. I’m not leaving.

1254
01:39:36,686 --> 01:39:38,718
Hey, if you stay here any longer...

1255
01:39:38,967 --> 01:39:41,485
I’ll reopen your old case
and put you behind bars!

1256
01:39:41,566 --> 01:39:43,358
I don't care.
At least I'll get to see my mother.

1257
01:39:43,439 --> 01:39:44,454
Take him out!

1258
01:39:45,564 --> 01:39:49,014
If I bring you the person you're after,
will you show me my mother?

1259
01:39:50,503 --> 01:39:51,303
Who?

1260
01:39:55,567 --> 01:39:58,319
I wasn’t the only one
who escaped from you back then...

1261
01:40:00,367 --> 01:40:01,773
there was someone else too, right?

1262
01:41:37,729 --> 01:41:38,656
Abbas?

1263
01:41:42,650 --> 01:41:44,138
Hold him. Hold him!

1264
01:41:44,218 --> 01:41:45,298
Yes, that’s it.

1265
01:41:47,130 --> 01:41:48,474
Who’s this boy?

1266
01:41:49,395 --> 01:41:51,538
He was in your lorry.
Don't you know him?

1267
01:41:51,891 --> 01:41:52,930
My lorry?

1268
01:41:53,218 --> 01:41:55,059
I don’t know. No idea!

1269
01:41:57,874 --> 01:42:00,307
He was inside when I got in,
so I thought he was with you.

1270
01:42:00,388 --> 01:42:01,915
-With me?
-Yeah.

1271
01:42:02,595 --> 01:42:03,859
Who are you?

1272
01:42:03,955 --> 01:42:05,475
Why did you sneak into the vehicle?

1273
01:42:05,562 --> 01:42:06,699
Trying to steal?

1274
01:42:07,258 --> 01:42:07,914
Huh!?

1275
01:42:11,322 --> 01:42:12,714
His eyes say it all.

1276
01:42:12,795 --> 01:42:14,217
He’s 100% a thief, I'm telling you!

1277
01:42:16,137 --> 01:42:17,875
So what do we do now?

1278
01:42:17,956 --> 01:42:19,827
What? He was in your lorry.
You deal with him.

1279
01:42:19,907 --> 01:42:22,234
-Abbas!
-We’ll see tomorrow.

1280
01:42:22,315 --> 01:42:23,242
Wait, man!

1281
01:42:25,529 --> 01:42:27,938
I’ll chop your legs off
if you trouble me again!

1282
01:42:28,018 --> 01:42:29,034
Get lost!

1283
01:42:29,418 --> 01:42:30,330
Go away!

1284
01:42:32,474 --> 01:42:33,578
I said go!

1285
01:43:01,348 --> 01:43:02,246
What do you want?

1286
01:43:03,502 --> 01:43:04,839
Why are you following me?

1287
01:43:07,486 --> 01:43:08,141
Go away!

1288
01:43:19,058 --> 01:43:20,674
Didn’t I tell you to leave already?

1289
01:43:23,778 --> 01:43:25,714
I’ll peg this at you, mind it! Run!

1290
01:44:03,442 --> 01:44:05,266
-Hey, Abbas!
-Sir?

1291
01:44:05,722 --> 01:44:07,563
What? Didn’t you see us?

1292
01:44:07,954 --> 01:44:08,835
I didn’t notice, sir.

1293
01:44:08,915 --> 01:44:09,754
What?

1294
01:44:09,835 --> 01:44:10,954
I didn’t notice, sir.

1295
01:44:11,043 --> 01:44:12,307
Where were you off stealing from?

1296
01:44:13,123 --> 01:44:14,626
Where did you go stealing?

1297
01:44:14,707 --> 01:44:16,018
I’m coming back from work, sir.

1298
01:44:16,419 --> 01:44:17,602
I’m coming back from work, sir.

1299
01:44:17,683 --> 01:44:19,411
I’m well aware of what
you’re up to at night!

1300
01:44:19,492 --> 01:44:21,427
What’s that? What’s in your pocket?

1301
01:44:24,187 --> 01:44:25,930
Just a phone, sir. Nothing else.

1302
01:44:29,331 --> 01:44:30,282
Nothing in the bag, sir.

1303
01:44:30,363 --> 01:44:31,794
-Is it?
-Nothing.

1304
01:44:32,955 --> 01:44:34,522
What did you throw there?

1305
01:44:34,713 --> 01:44:36,329
What did you dump over there?

1306
01:44:36,795 --> 01:44:37,915
Just waste.

1307
01:44:37,996 --> 01:44:39,771
Waste? What waste?

1308
01:44:40,123 --> 01:44:41,242
Food waste.

1309
01:44:41,354 --> 01:44:42,187
Show me.

1310
01:44:42,268 --> 01:44:43,587
-Show me.
-Sir, it’s just food waste.

1311
01:44:43,923 --> 01:44:45,027
Show me. Come.

1312
01:44:45,178 --> 01:44:46,539
-Walk!
-It’s just food waste, sir.

1313
01:44:47,443 --> 01:44:48,979
Check it.

1314
01:44:49,579 --> 01:44:50,458
Search!

1315
01:44:53,259 --> 01:44:54,075
Look there.

1316
01:45:00,314 --> 01:45:01,481
Why do you look nervous?

1317
01:45:02,121 --> 01:45:03,914
Nervous? Why would I be nervous, sir?

1318
01:45:04,396 --> 01:45:05,155
Just waste, sir.

1319
01:45:05,236 --> 01:45:07,267
Waste? I know. Look properly.

1320
01:45:10,883 --> 01:45:12,788
Nothing, sir. Just waste.

1321
01:45:12,907 --> 01:45:13,706
Really?

1322
01:45:13,954 --> 01:45:14,866
Let’s go then.

1323
01:45:16,618 --> 01:45:18,026
Told you, sir.

1324
01:45:18,146 --> 01:45:19,546
You suspected me for nothing.

1325
01:45:20,355 --> 01:45:21,891
You’re messing around in Kerala, huh?

1326
01:45:22,234 --> 01:45:23,835
I’ll nab you here one day.

1327
01:45:23,915 --> 01:45:26,523
And when I do,
I'll just rip you apart!

1328
01:45:26,603 --> 01:45:27,435
Go!

1329
01:45:32,659 --> 01:45:33,442
Go!

1330
01:46:20,018 --> 01:46:20,937
Give it!

1331
01:46:32,505 --> 01:46:33,690
You...

1332
01:46:34,154 --> 01:46:36,122
So you really are a thief, huh?

1333
01:46:37,889 --> 01:46:39,074
Thank you.

1334
01:46:44,633 --> 01:46:45,945
Here, keep it.

1335
01:46:47,849 --> 01:46:48,713
Take it.

1336
01:46:49,424 --> 01:46:50,192
No need?

1337
01:46:50,913 --> 01:46:52,385
Fine then!

1338
01:46:53,154 --> 01:46:54,402
So what do you want?

1339
01:46:54,483 --> 01:46:55,185
Huh?

1340
01:46:56,322 --> 01:46:57,506
Mom!

1341
01:46:57,889 --> 01:46:58,633
What?

1342
01:47:07,050 --> 01:47:08,139
So...

1343
01:47:09,234 --> 01:47:11,970
your mom didn’t come to
pick you up after school.

1344
01:47:12,946 --> 01:47:14,691
Then the police caught you.

1345
01:47:16,050 --> 01:47:18,610
You escaped from them, got into a lorry...

1346
01:47:18,691 --> 01:47:19,971
and ended up here.

1347
01:47:20,394 --> 01:47:21,178
Right?

1348
01:47:22,138 --> 01:47:23,002
Okay.

1349
01:47:25,666 --> 01:47:27,603
Remember where you got into the lorry?

1350
01:47:28,938 --> 01:47:29,962
No.

1351
01:47:31,146 --> 01:47:33,290
Do you have any idea where this place is?

1352
01:47:33,946 --> 01:47:35,130
No, not that either.

1353
01:47:38,370 --> 01:47:39,474
Wait...

1354
01:47:41,170 --> 01:47:43,330
Why did you run away from the police?

1355
01:47:43,411 --> 01:47:46,099
If you had stayed,
they would’ve taken you to your mom.

1356
01:47:46,722 --> 01:47:47,523
Hmm?

1357
01:47:51,202 --> 01:47:53,298
Something’s totally off about you, huh?

1358
01:47:54,738 --> 01:47:56,163
What’s your name?

1359
01:47:58,121 --> 01:48:00,817
Tell me your name.
I need something to call you, right?

1360
01:48:01,802 --> 01:48:02,714
Let me see.

1361
01:48:02,961 --> 01:48:04,610
Who does this belong to?

1362
01:48:04,690 --> 01:48:06,322
Pa-vi-thran...

1363
01:48:07,970 --> 01:48:09,089
Pavithran?

1364
01:48:09,330 --> 01:48:10,274
That works.

1365
01:48:11,186 --> 01:48:12,082
Good name.

1366
01:48:13,240 --> 01:48:14,185
Sister!

1367
01:48:14,551 --> 01:48:16,200
-Sister?
-Yes?

1368
01:48:16,280 --> 01:48:17,448
Is there anything to eat?

1369
01:48:17,528 --> 01:48:19,183
-Yes.
-Then serve it.

1370
01:48:19,841 --> 01:48:21,393
Serve for two.

1371
01:48:24,505 --> 01:48:25,337
Do you bathe?

1372
01:48:33,217 --> 01:48:34,913
Who is this kid!?

1373
01:48:35,721 --> 01:48:37,586
That’s Pavithran.

1374
01:48:37,666 --> 01:48:40,802
What are you up to,
bringing kids here from Kerala?

1375
01:48:40,882 --> 01:48:43,641
Listen, Abbas.
Hand him over to the police.

1376
01:48:43,722 --> 01:48:44,985
Oh, great!

1377
01:48:45,066 --> 01:48:47,105
He escaped from the police and came here!

1378
01:48:48,721 --> 01:48:50,864
Wait till morning.
I’ll send him back in a fish vehicle.

1379
01:48:51,146 --> 01:48:53,465
You never listen to a word I say!

1380
01:48:53,546 --> 01:48:55,376
-Sister, serve the rice.
-Yeah, I will.

1381
01:48:57,984 --> 01:48:58,976
Hey!

1382
01:48:59,865 --> 01:49:02,137
Good thing you escaped from the police.

1383
01:49:02,217 --> 01:49:03,618
They’re just a bunch of thieves!

1384
01:49:08,383 --> 01:49:09,679
Don’t worry.

1385
01:49:09,840 --> 01:49:11,247
You want to find your mom, right?

1386
01:49:11,328 --> 01:49:12,080
Consider it done!

1387
01:49:12,161 --> 01:49:13,584
First thing in the morning!

1388
01:49:17,065 --> 01:49:18,345
Hey, Abbas!

1389
01:49:18,426 --> 01:49:20,025
Wake up! It’s already evening.

1390
01:49:20,106 --> 01:49:21,545
Are you going to sleep all day?

1391
01:49:36,530 --> 01:49:37,905
Who are you?

1392
01:49:38,937 --> 01:49:40,730
Mr Pavithran!

1393
01:49:42,146 --> 01:49:43,433
You woke up early?

1394
01:49:44,441 --> 01:49:46,281
How's our place?

1395
01:49:46,362 --> 01:49:47,481
Do you like it?

1396
01:49:50,960 --> 01:49:52,688
Say something, boy.

1397
01:49:53,313 --> 01:49:54,313
Mom...

1398
01:49:55,490 --> 01:49:56,178
Mom?

1399
01:49:57,530 --> 01:49:58,393
That’s what bothers you.

1400
01:49:58,473 --> 01:49:59,417
Let's sort it out.

1401
01:50:00,370 --> 01:50:02,466
Let's sort it out.

1402
01:50:05,801 --> 01:50:06,842
Listen...

1403
01:50:06,922 --> 01:50:09,098
Take this boy back to where he belongs.

1404
01:50:09,689 --> 01:50:11,497
He was crying all night.

1405
01:50:11,577 --> 01:50:13,417
But he has to tell me something first.

1406
01:50:13,497 --> 01:50:14,409
Let’s see.

1407
01:50:30,033 --> 01:50:31,521
Do you brush your teeth?

1408
01:50:32,969 --> 01:50:34,297
Show me your hand.

1409
01:50:39,561 --> 01:50:41,066
What’s your mom’s name again?

1410
01:50:43,817 --> 01:50:45,401
Leave it. Brush first.

1411
01:51:04,018 --> 01:51:05,043
Udbhav?

1412
01:51:05,123 --> 01:51:06,163
Pavi...

1413
01:51:06,244 --> 01:51:07,475
Food’s ready.

1414
01:51:07,556 --> 01:51:08,483
Come eat.

1415
01:51:12,569 --> 01:51:13,658
Don’t worry.

1416
01:51:13,738 --> 01:51:15,225
Abbas has gone looking for your mom.

1417
01:51:15,322 --> 01:51:16,082
They’ll be back tomorrow.

1418
01:51:16,162 --> 01:51:16,994
Come inside now.

1419
01:51:17,074 --> 01:51:18,081
Come on!

1420
01:51:55,402 --> 01:51:57,210
Here, I bought this for you.

1421
01:51:57,890 --> 01:51:59,138
It's clothes.

1422
01:52:01,555 --> 01:52:02,883
No luck at all.

1423
01:52:02,963 --> 01:52:04,403
I searched everywhere for her.

1424
01:52:05,481 --> 01:52:06,825
It’ll take a lot of effort.

1425
01:52:07,611 --> 01:52:08,651
Hold this.

1426
01:52:08,732 --> 01:52:09,781
Come on.

1427
01:52:12,435 --> 01:52:13,474
See?

1428
01:52:13,555 --> 01:52:14,931
Look how much this costs.

1429
01:52:16,178 --> 01:52:18,322
Finding your mom will cost money too.

1430
01:52:18,730 --> 01:52:20,427
We’ll have to work for it.

1431
01:52:20,507 --> 01:52:21,171
For that...

1432
01:52:21,251 --> 01:52:22,659
you need to learn first.

1433
01:52:25,657 --> 01:52:27,905
And there’s a perfect
place to start learning.

1434
01:52:40,492 --> 01:52:42,802
-Pay the money and play.
-I’ll pay it.

1435
01:52:42,883 --> 01:52:44,474
-Didn’t you say that yesterday?
-I will give you.

1436
01:52:44,554 --> 01:52:46,314
-I will.
-When exactly!?

1437
01:52:46,395 --> 01:52:47,937
I’ll give you the money.

1438
01:52:50,396 --> 01:52:51,596
Oh, hey.

1439
01:52:51,677 --> 01:52:53,658
-He’s with you now?
-Poor boy. Come.

1440
01:52:53,739 --> 01:52:54,860
Boss is over there.

1441
01:52:59,779 --> 01:53:00,595
Boss...

1442
01:53:03,364 --> 01:53:04,660
Who’s this boy?

1443
01:53:04,746 --> 01:53:05,620
My sister’s son.

1444
01:53:05,700 --> 01:53:06,852
Is that so?

1445
01:53:07,188 --> 01:53:08,963
Seems like you have many sisters.

1446
01:53:09,173 --> 01:53:10,596
What’s his name?

1447
01:53:10,677 --> 01:53:11,556
Pavithran...

1448
01:53:11,637 --> 01:53:12,693
Pavi.

1449
01:53:12,774 --> 01:53:14,629
-Pavithra?
-Pavi!

1450
01:53:16,308 --> 01:53:17,492
Take this.

1451
01:53:17,901 --> 01:53:20,460
Take it! Give it to table number four.

1452
01:53:23,068 --> 01:53:24,316
-Udbhav!
-Coming!

1453
01:53:25,252 --> 01:53:26,276
Are you new here?

1454
01:53:33,360 --> 01:53:35,610
♪ O' my son ♪

1455
01:53:38,143 --> 01:53:40,880
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1456
01:53:40,964 --> 01:53:43,097
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1457
01:53:43,260 --> 01:53:44,146
Like a key!

1458
01:53:44,230 --> 01:53:47,063
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1459
01:53:47,147 --> 01:53:50,533
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1460
01:53:51,602 --> 01:53:58,018
♪ You bloom like the night ♪

1461
01:53:58,102 --> 01:53:59,370
♪ O' my son ♪

1462
01:54:06,759 --> 01:54:07,597
Abbas...

1463
01:54:07,858 --> 01:54:08,500
Boss?

1464
01:54:08,580 --> 01:54:10,932
You've trained him well.

1465
01:54:11,673 --> 01:54:13,274
He's got the hang of it.

1466
01:54:13,996 --> 01:54:17,597
Smart kids like him are
hard to find these days.

1467
01:54:17,677 --> 01:54:19,213
Can you sell him to me?

1468
01:54:19,294 --> 01:54:20,574
Not for sale, boss.

1469
01:54:20,990 --> 01:54:23,022
Since when did you turn into such a saint?

1470
01:54:34,734 --> 01:54:35,421
Let's go.

1471
01:54:51,946 --> 01:54:54,698
♪ Is it the dew in those brimming eyes? ♪

1472
01:54:54,818 --> 01:54:57,683
♪ Or the radiance in that waning smile? ♪

1473
01:54:57,764 --> 01:54:59,108
Your hometown...

1474
01:54:59,413 --> 01:55:00,148
Is it in the forest...

1475
01:55:00,228 --> 01:55:01,948
or somewhere by the backwaters?

1476
01:55:02,093 --> 01:55:02,916
Any idea?

1477
01:55:05,190 --> 01:55:06,934
Do you at least remember your school?

1478
01:55:07,014 --> 01:55:08,550
Little Flower!

1479
01:55:08,924 --> 01:55:10,205
Oh, great!

1480
01:55:10,285 --> 01:55:12,238
There are countless Little Flower
schools in Kerala.

1481
01:55:12,318 --> 01:55:13,809
There’s even one in
the town of Irinjalakuda.

1482
01:55:14,573 --> 01:55:16,013
See that building?

1483
01:55:16,354 --> 01:55:17,266
Superb, right?

1484
01:55:49,317 --> 01:55:50,213
Good boy!

1485
01:55:50,297 --> 01:55:53,047
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1486
01:55:53,131 --> 01:55:56,307
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1487
01:55:56,391 --> 01:55:59,127
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1488
01:55:59,211 --> 01:56:02,317
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1489
01:56:02,401 --> 01:56:05,203
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1490
01:56:05,287 --> 01:56:08,423
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1491
01:56:08,507 --> 01:56:11,427
♪ O son, my son, my dearest one ♪

1492
01:56:12,970 --> 01:56:14,058
Give it to him.

1493
01:56:19,466 --> 01:56:20,490
Don't worry.

1494
01:56:20,571 --> 01:56:21,770
He's one of ours.

1495
01:56:21,850 --> 01:56:22,618
Go give it.

1496
01:56:23,226 --> 01:56:24,058
Go.

1497
01:56:28,354 --> 01:56:31,282
This isn’t enough.
You’ll have to pay more.

1498
01:56:41,027 --> 01:56:41,865
Sister...

1499
01:56:41,946 --> 01:56:42,777
Get me something to eat.

1500
01:56:42,858 --> 01:56:44,496
Here, give it to him quickly.

1501
01:56:44,642 --> 01:56:45,892
Go, hurry up!

1502
01:56:50,268 --> 01:56:53,036
No one’s here to serve
the fish fry I asked for!?

1503
01:56:55,011 --> 01:56:55,956
Huh?

1504
01:56:56,228 --> 01:56:57,572
Hey...

1505
01:56:57,652 --> 01:56:59,732
-Aren’t you happy?
-Happy, happy.

1506
01:57:00,860 --> 01:57:01,868
Give it!

1507
01:57:01,948 --> 01:57:03,404
How long have I been asking?

1508
01:57:10,082 --> 01:57:11,186
You’re cool.

1509
01:57:11,547 --> 01:57:13,004
I like you.

1510
01:57:13,827 --> 01:57:14,787
You...

1511
01:57:15,051 --> 01:57:16,395
You can just stay here.

1512
01:57:16,556 --> 01:57:17,867
Be one of my boys.

1513
01:57:18,740 --> 01:57:20,036
Let’s rule together!

1514
01:57:20,468 --> 01:57:21,788
What about my mom?

1515
01:57:22,610 --> 01:57:24,067
Did you hear him?

1516
01:57:24,291 --> 01:57:26,506
Forget your mom.
You've got Abba now.

1517
01:57:30,115 --> 01:57:31,395
I understand...

1518
01:57:31,476 --> 01:57:33,237
I understand your feelings.

1519
01:57:35,155 --> 01:57:36,179
I will...

1520
01:57:36,436 --> 01:57:38,548
I’ll take you to your mom.

1521
01:57:40,835 --> 01:57:42,643
I’ll do it at any cost!

1522
01:57:42,723 --> 01:57:43,635
Got it?

1523
01:57:43,716 --> 01:57:44,795
Stop me, if you dare!

1524
01:57:45,308 --> 01:57:47,195
No one on earth can!

1525
01:57:48,331 --> 01:57:49,339
That’s...

1526
01:57:49,419 --> 01:57:50,484
my power.

1527
01:57:54,484 --> 01:57:55,956
I'll find your mom.

1528
01:58:33,651 --> 01:58:34,851
What happened?

1529
01:58:40,156 --> 01:58:40,940
Hmm?

1530
01:58:42,732 --> 01:58:44,619
Stop staring and tell me!

1531
01:58:45,083 --> 01:58:47,114
They've been calling me from Bangalore.

1532
01:58:47,356 --> 01:58:48,732
There’s a job.

1533
01:58:48,813 --> 01:58:49,803
A pretty big deal.

1534
01:58:49,884 --> 01:58:50,988
A big deal?

1535
01:58:51,459 --> 01:58:52,916
What big deal?

1536
01:58:55,216 --> 01:58:56,448
So, you've become a big-shot now!?

1537
01:58:56,948 --> 01:58:59,060
You’re not going anywhere.
Stay right here.

1538
01:59:00,579 --> 01:59:02,771
How long are we supposed
to rot here, Abba?

1539
01:59:04,179 --> 01:59:06,323
Only the two of us are left here.

1540
01:59:06,621 --> 01:59:07,677
So what?

1541
01:59:08,276 --> 01:59:10,371
At least let me go, Abba.

1542
01:59:11,508 --> 01:59:12,548
You want to go?

1543
01:59:12,884 --> 01:59:13,700
Huh?

1544
01:59:23,308 --> 01:59:26,883
I didn’t raise you all these years
to go work for strangers!

1545
01:59:27,620 --> 01:59:29,427
Do you have even a little gratitude?

1546
01:59:30,740 --> 01:59:32,547
You want to find your mom, right?

1547
01:59:33,091 --> 01:59:35,196
How will that happen if you roam
around Bangalore and Mysore?

1548
01:59:35,277 --> 01:59:37,500
-Please listen to me--
-You listen to me!

1549
01:59:52,188 --> 01:59:53,820
Nothing to eat here!?

1550
01:59:56,476 --> 01:59:58,140
Go buy something! Damn!

1551
02:00:24,675 --> 02:00:25,860
Yes, boss?

1552
02:00:32,762 --> 02:00:34,331
I’m coming. I’m coming.

1553
02:00:47,324 --> 02:00:49,812
Where the hell were you?
Get this nuisance out of here!

1554
02:00:49,893 --> 02:00:52,724
I've told him a hundred times
not to act mad when he's drunk!

1555
02:00:52,804 --> 02:00:55,412
Better take him away
or you'll get beaten too!

1556
02:00:57,515 --> 02:01:00,299
Want some more slaps, you dog!? Stay put!

1557
02:01:15,042 --> 02:01:16,626
I’m leaving!

1558
02:01:19,561 --> 02:01:20,713
Will you?

1559
02:01:21,434 --> 02:01:22,699
Then what about your mom?

1560
02:01:22,779 --> 02:01:24,626
Stop bringing that up all the time!

1561
02:01:24,723 --> 02:01:26,844
I know you just can't do it!

1562
02:01:28,354 --> 02:01:29,490
Then go ahead.

1563
02:01:29,778 --> 02:01:30,961
Go!

1564
02:01:33,049 --> 02:01:34,681
All of you can go!

1565
02:01:35,761 --> 02:01:36,705
Hey...

1566
02:01:37,338 --> 02:01:38,554
You fool...

1567
02:01:38,635 --> 02:01:40,699
Your mom abandoned you!

1568
02:01:41,986 --> 02:01:43,707
And I was the only one there for you!

1569
02:01:43,788 --> 02:01:45,627
Abbas was the only one there for you!

1570
02:01:46,211 --> 02:01:48,194
And now you pushed me?

1571
02:02:26,644 --> 02:02:27,525
Hey?

1572
02:02:29,061 --> 02:02:29,988
What’s wrong?

1573
02:02:30,069 --> 02:02:31,356
Are you upset with me?

1574
02:02:37,252 --> 02:02:38,900
When are you heading to Bangalore?

1575
02:02:43,515 --> 02:02:44,115
Listen…

1576
02:02:44,540 --> 02:02:46,108
Shall we do one last job?

1577
02:02:49,796 --> 02:02:51,476
You’ll need money for
Bangalore too, right?

1578
02:02:52,588 --> 02:02:54,060
I’m sick of this place.

1579
02:02:58,430 --> 02:02:59,374
Please…

1580
02:03:00,714 --> 02:03:01,979
Just one last job.

1581
02:03:03,364 --> 02:03:04,021
For me.

1582
02:03:11,884 --> 02:03:13,036
Let’s go tomorrow.

1583
02:03:13,772 --> 02:03:14,412
Tomorrow, okay?

1584
02:03:14,493 --> 02:03:15,244
Come with me.

1585
02:03:56,218 --> 02:03:56,906
Hey!

1586
02:03:56,987 --> 02:03:58,234
Where the hell were you?

1587
02:03:58,363 --> 02:04:00,251
Didn’t we have a job to finish?

1588
02:04:08,100 --> 02:04:08,868
Hey!

1589
02:04:09,044 --> 02:04:10,500
Where did you go?

1590
02:04:10,620 --> 02:04:12,732
Why did you disappear
without telling anyone?

1591
02:04:14,676 --> 02:04:16,339
Because you were furious with me!?

1592
02:04:16,965 --> 02:04:18,612
Look what he's done!

1593
02:04:19,764 --> 02:04:21,764
Do you know what work we came here for?

1594
02:04:23,756 --> 02:04:24,828
Do you?

1595
02:04:28,828 --> 02:04:30,172
You idiot...

1596
02:04:30,692 --> 02:04:32,196
we found your mom!

1597
02:04:32,676 --> 02:04:33,876
For real!

1598
02:04:35,540 --> 02:04:36,419
Actually...

1599
02:04:36,500 --> 02:04:39,122
a few days after you first came here...

1600
02:04:39,203 --> 02:04:40,132
I went to Kerala...

1601
02:04:40,213 --> 02:04:42,140
and made inquiries about you and your mom.

1602
02:04:42,220 --> 02:04:43,804
That’s when I found out...

1603
02:04:43,885 --> 02:04:45,724
that your mom was in jail.

1604
02:04:46,187 --> 02:04:48,059
How could I send you back
without your mom?

1605
02:04:48,140 --> 02:04:49,571
So I thought...

1606
02:04:49,652 --> 02:04:51,339
once her sentence was over,

1607
02:04:51,555 --> 02:04:53,507
I’d take you to her as a surprise.

1608
02:04:53,588 --> 02:04:54,588
It was a perfect plan.

1609
02:04:54,908 --> 02:04:55,754
But that didn’t work.

1610
02:04:56,059 --> 02:04:57,530
Your mother...

1611
02:04:57,611 --> 02:04:58,771
they...

1612
02:04:58,851 --> 02:05:00,602
they moved her to a mental hospital.

1613
02:05:00,937 --> 02:05:01,994
Only recently...

1614
02:05:02,075 --> 02:05:04,939
I found out that a cop named
Pavithran took her from there.

1615
02:05:06,381 --> 02:05:08,205
Who is this other Pavithran?

1616
02:05:08,285 --> 02:05:09,205
Abbas!

1617
02:05:10,691 --> 02:05:11,795
Police!

1618
02:05:19,980 --> 02:05:21,291
Hurry up, Abba!

1619
02:05:21,372 --> 02:05:22,443
No need.

1620
02:05:22,932 --> 02:05:24,420
They must be all around.

1621
02:05:35,188 --> 02:05:36,676
-Hey!
-Let go of me!

1622
02:05:41,421 --> 02:05:42,636
Abbas...

1623
02:05:42,717 --> 02:05:43,932
All good?

1624
02:05:45,052 --> 02:05:46,989
So this is the real Pavithran, right?

1625
02:05:49,316 --> 02:05:50,547
Put your hands out.

1626
02:05:50,947 --> 02:05:52,787
Why the hurry?

1627
02:05:52,868 --> 02:05:54,388
Couldn’t you have waited a bit longer?

1628
02:05:54,469 --> 02:05:55,852
Why didn't you tell
me this earlier, Abba!?

1629
02:05:55,933 --> 02:05:56,974
And then what?

1630
02:05:57,054 --> 02:05:58,420
So you could send me to jail?

1631
02:05:58,501 --> 02:05:59,893
Move, move!

1632
02:06:02,795 --> 02:06:04,443
What was going through your head!?

1633
02:06:04,524 --> 02:06:06,875
Do you really think he’d
take you to your mom?

1634
02:06:09,996 --> 02:06:11,628
-Sorry, sir.
-What the hell!

1635
02:06:11,709 --> 02:06:13,500
My plan was just perfect!

1636
02:06:13,581 --> 02:06:14,844
I made a mistake, Abba.

1637
02:06:15,948 --> 02:06:17,116
Take him!

1638
02:06:17,197 --> 02:06:18,300
Move!

1639
02:06:18,939 --> 02:06:20,275
It's for your birth mother.

1640
02:06:20,355 --> 02:06:22,068
Your foster father can take the fall.

1641
02:06:22,149 --> 02:06:23,643
-Right, sir?
-Walk!

1642
02:06:24,297 --> 02:06:25,897
No need to pull me, sir.
I'm not going anywhere.

1643
02:06:27,117 --> 02:06:29,350
-Get in!
-Alright, alright!

1644
02:06:43,789 --> 02:06:45,916
Can’t you at least give my mom back now?

1645
02:06:47,437 --> 02:06:49,501
I'm never giving her back.

1646
02:06:51,292 --> 02:06:53,212
Just like I never got my Cicily.

1647
02:06:55,484 --> 02:06:57,100
But I'll let you see her.

1648
02:06:57,268 --> 02:06:58,420
Only once.

1649
02:06:59,485 --> 02:07:00,637
Take it as proof.

1650
02:07:50,620 --> 02:07:51,340
Come.

1651
02:07:58,036 --> 02:08:00,644
You still remember her as
that beautiful mother, huh?

1652
02:08:04,221 --> 02:08:05,885
She’s in the last cell.

1653
02:08:06,396 --> 02:08:07,708
Go take a good look!

1654
02:08:20,124 --> 02:08:21,084
Go on.

1655
02:09:01,660 --> 02:09:02,428
Mom...

1656
02:09:05,269 --> 02:09:06,181
Mom!

1657
02:11:04,749 --> 02:11:08,140
They're the ones who killed your son!

1658
02:11:13,976 --> 02:11:16,090
♪ Where are you off to, like the wind? ♪

1659
02:11:16,174 --> 02:11:18,413
♪ Where are you off to, like the cloud? ♪

1660
02:11:18,643 --> 02:11:23,077
♪ Is it to reap the great rain
from the fields of the sky? ♪

1661
02:11:23,161 --> 02:11:25,543
♪ O hands, feet, and eyes, ♪

1662
02:11:25,627 --> 02:11:27,920
♪ Where are you all off to? ♪

1663
02:11:28,004 --> 02:11:32,457
♪ Chasing the fleeting deer, a mirage? ♪

1664
02:11:32,783 --> 02:11:35,050
♪ Where do all these roads lead? ♪

1665
02:11:35,134 --> 02:11:37,280
♪ Stretching on and on, where to? ♪

1666
02:11:37,527 --> 02:11:39,730
♪ To the very edge of the earth, ♪

1667
02:11:39,814 --> 02:11:41,893
♪ Seeking the bright moonlight? ♪

1668
02:11:42,090 --> 02:11:46,683
♪ Swaying like a milkweed seed, ♪

1669
02:11:46,767 --> 02:11:48,817
♪ Where are you off to? ♪

1670
02:11:48,901 --> 02:11:51,373
♪ Unseen by anyone else? ♪

1671
02:11:51,457 --> 02:11:55,110
♪ Where are you drifting away? ♪

1672
02:11:56,057 --> 02:11:58,173
♪ You, fallen leaf? ♪

1673
02:12:14,628 --> 02:12:16,965
From now on, however late I may be...

1674
02:12:17,045 --> 02:12:18,916
leave not this place.

1675
02:12:19,753 --> 02:12:21,287
Remain here.

1676
02:12:22,597 --> 02:12:24,080
Mother will come!

1677
02:14:17,548 --> 02:14:19,309
Didn’t I tell you...

1678
02:14:20,461 --> 02:14:22,573
to stay right here
no matter how late I get?

1679
02:14:28,428 --> 02:14:30,381
What’s our new story, Mom?

1680
02:14:32,813 --> 02:14:33,501
I’ll tell you.

1681
02:14:38,493 --> 02:14:40,701
And what’s my new name?

